WEBVTT


00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:59.090
Are you watching closely?


00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:10.390
Every magic trick consistsNof three parts, or acts.


00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.870
The first part is called "the pledge".


00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:17.310
The magician shows youNsomething ordinary.


00:01:17.380 --> 00:01:20.840
A deck of cards, a bird or a man.


00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:29.890
He shows you this object.


00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.550
Perhaps he asks you to inspect it,


00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:35.650
to see that it is indeed real,


00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.790
unaltered, normal.


00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.340
But, of course, it probably isn't.


00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:47.200
Where do you think you're going?


00:01:47.270 --> 00:01:49.640
I'm part of the bloody act, you fool.


00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:05.020
The second act is called "the turn".


00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:22.530
The magician takesNthe ordinary something


00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:27.200
and makes it doNsomething extraordinary.


00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:35.810
Now you're looking for theNsecret, but you won't find it,


00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:39.720
because, of course,Nyou're not really looking.


00:02:39.790 --> 00:02:41.420
You don't really want to know.


00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:47.060
You want to be... fooled.


00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:51.170
But you wouldn't clap yet,


00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:55.400
because making somethingNdisappear isn't enough.


00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:59.070
You have to bring it back.


00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:04.350
That's why every magic trickNhas a third act.


00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:06.080
The hardest part.


00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.680
The part we call...


00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:10.090
...".the prestige".


00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:25.070
The prestige? And did RobertNAngier, the Great Danton, your employer,


00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:27.570
get to that final partNof his trick that night?


00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:29.730
- No, sir. Something went wrong.N- What went wrong?


00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:34.400
I saw someone makingNtheir way below stage.


00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.380
I followed him.


00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:39.710
It was Borden,Nwatching Mr. Angier drown.


00:03:39.790 --> 00:03:43.220
Would you please describeNyour occupation to the jury, Mr. Cutter.


00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.660
I'm an ingénieur, I design illusions


00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:48.890
and construct the apparatusNnecessary for performing them.


00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:53.400
So, Mr. Cutter, was thisNwater-filled tank beneath the stage


00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:55.060
part of Mr. Angier's illusion?


00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:59.000
No. The tank was broughtNon for the first trick


00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:01.040
and then taken offstage.


00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:04.410
Borden must have placed itNunder the trap door after the end of it.


00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.040
How large was this tank?


00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:08.710
It's a normal tankNfor escape under water,


00:04:08.780 --> 00:04:10.910
about 400 or 500 gallons.


00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:13.470
How do you think heNwas able to move the tank


00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:15.920
under the trap doorNwithout anyone noticing?


00:04:15.990 --> 00:04:18.350
He's a magician, ask him.


00:04:18.420 --> 00:04:19.520
I ask again,


00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:22.820
would this man explain the mechanicsNof Mr. Angier's illusion.


00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:26.230
The Real Transported Man is oneNof the most sought after illusions


00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.490
in this business.


00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:29.130
I have the right to sell it on.


00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.830
If I reveal the method here,Nthe trick is worthless.


00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:34.170
How can we knowNthat the tank wasn't simply


00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:36.710
some part of the trick that went wrong?


00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:38.840
Mr. Cutter, I see your predicament.


00:04:38.910 --> 00:04:41.310
But Alfred Borden's lifeNhangs in the balance.


00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.540
If you were prepared to discloseNthe details to me in private,


00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:47.450
I might be able to judgeNtheir relevance to the case.


00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:50.150
Might this be an acceptable compromise?


00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:11.810
I'm going to have to askNyou to turn out your pockets.


00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:19.510
Not my idea, sir. The warden sawNhis show in Manchester last year


00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.450
where he vanished into thin air.


00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:24.010
He's convinced he'll try and escape.


00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:30.220
I told him the only wayNBorden's going to disappear


00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.730
is if I leave him out thereNwith the other inmates.


00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:39.940
Check the locks...


00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:43.200
...twice.


00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.810
My name is Owens.


00:05:52.890 --> 00:05:55.150
I'm a solicitor.


00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:58.880
I represent Lord Caldlow, anNaccomplished amateur magician and...


00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:01.550
How much?


00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:03.960
- He is interested...N- How much for my tricks?


00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.620
Five thousand pounds.


00:06:05.700 --> 00:06:08.190
Talk to Fallon, my ingénieur.NMoney's for him.


00:06:08.270 --> 00:06:11.960
Yes, I did. He offeredNto sell me your tricks.


00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:14.910
All except the most valuableNone, The Transported Man.


00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:18.270
Well, I won't forgive myselfNfor selling my greatest trick.


00:06:18.340 --> 00:06:19.780
Even for your daughter?


00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:25.780
If you are for the drop, your daughterNis going to need looking after.


00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:27.580
Fallon will take care of her.


00:06:27.650 --> 00:06:29.380
Perfect, Fallon.


00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:31.480
A man with a pastNas obscure as your own.


00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:36.590
The courts have motioned she be removedNfrom his care. She will be an orphan.


00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.930
I know you're no strangerNto the workhouse.


00:06:39.700 --> 00:06:41.530
It's better than here?


00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:44.830
I'm offering you a way to wrap upNyour affairs with dignity.


00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:46.870
I'm offering your daughter a future.


00:06:46.940 --> 00:06:49.970
As Lord Caldlow's ward,Nshe will want for nothing...


00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:51.870
...ever.


00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:54.940
Well, think it over.


00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:58.780
And Lord CaldlowNwould like you to have this,


00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:01.380
as a show of good faith.NIt might be of interest.


00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:04.980
Robert Angier's diary, includingNthe time he spent in Colorado


00:07:05.060 --> 00:07:06.320
Iearning your trick.


00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:08.090
- He never learned it.N- Really?


00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:11.690
On his return, he mountedNa version of The Transported Man


00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:15.720
that the papers said wasNbetter even than your original.


00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:17.100
If you want Angier's secrets,


00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:22.630
you go dig him up and ask him yourself.


00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:24.570
I want your secret, Mr. Borden.


00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:28.950
Consider your daughter.


00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:38.360
A cipher,


00:07:38.420 --> 00:07:40.450
an enigma...


00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:44.190
...a search,


00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:45.250
a search for answers.


00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:56.740
Even if ColoradoNis the end of my journey,


00:07:56.810 --> 00:08:00.010
it'll take much longer to unravel


00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.980
the rest of Borden's secrets.


00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:06.020
See, the cipher in his notebook is


00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:08.580
unlocked by a single word,


00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:11.620
but it will still take monthsNto translate his writing.


00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:14.460
And to know his mind.


00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.730
Well, my passion is equal to the task.


00:08:32.810 --> 00:08:36.340
Mr. Angier, welcomeNto Colorado Springs.


00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:54.790
- The whole town has electricity.N- Yes, sir.


00:09:11.980 --> 00:09:13.470
Well...


00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:15.040
...quite a reception.


00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:17.610
You're our first guestNof the season, Mr. Angier.


00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:21.180
Your telegram didn't indicateNhow long you'd be staying with us.


00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:22.890
As long as it takes.


00:09:22.960 --> 00:09:26.230
I will need a coach tomorrowNto take me up the mountain.


00:09:26.300 --> 00:09:28.030
Well, the peak's closed, sir.


00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.930
For scientific experimentation.


00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.970
Yes, I know.


00:09:32.040 --> 00:09:33.330
That's why I'm here.


00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:42.810
Whoa. Whoa.


00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:47.450
You'll have to walkNthe rest, I'm afraid, sir.


00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:26.220
I'm amazed how manyNof you newspaper writers


00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:28.350
can't read my sign.


00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:35.690
Not the welcome I was expecting.


00:10:38.670 --> 00:10:40.730
I know you.


00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:46.230
You're the Great Danton.


00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:48.610
I saw your show in London.


00:10:48.680 --> 00:10:51.450
Seven times you guessed every object


00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:53.750
the audience had in their pockets.


00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:57.880
I'm Alley. Sorry about the fence.NPeople keep interfering with our work.


00:10:57.960 --> 00:11:00.620
- I've come to see Tesla.N- Why?


00:11:00.690 --> 00:11:04.750
He made a machineNfor a colleague of mine some time ago.


00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:08.320
- Can you get me a meeting with him?N- Impossible, I'm afraid.


00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:10.630
I've brought a lot of money.


00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:12.360
I'm sorry, Mr. Angier.


00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:15.100
I simply can't help.


00:11:17.180 --> 00:11:20.300
I'll be stayingNat the hotel, indefinitely.


00:11:23.650 --> 00:11:25.740
Hey, what am I holding?


00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:27.120
Your watch.


00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:35.420
Borden's journalNentry for April 3,1897,


00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:37.590
describes a showNat the Orpheum Theatre.


00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:40.560
That was just daysNafter he first met me.


00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:46.670
We were two young menNat the start of a great career,


00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:49.070
two young men devoted to an illusion,


00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:51.700
two young men who neverNintended to hurt anyone.


00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:53.540
Which of you brave souls


00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:56.340
is willing to bindNthis lovely young woman?


00:11:58.120 --> 00:12:00.050
Me!


00:12:08.530 --> 00:12:10.050
If you would tie her wrists,


00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:13.030
bind her feet...


00:12:13.100 --> 00:12:15.620
...around the ankle.


00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:17.790
Are either of you two gentlemen sailors?


00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:19.700
- No.N- No.


00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:23.600
I'm sure you can both tie a strong knot.


00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:30.300
He's complacent,Nhe's predictable, he's boring.


00:13:30.380 --> 00:13:32.940
Milton has gotten success,Nwhatever that means,


00:13:33.010 --> 00:13:36.240
so now he's scared.NHe won't take any risks at all.


00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:39.380
He's squandering the goodwillNof his audience with tired,


00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:42.050
- second-rate tricks...N- They're all favorites.


00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:45.610
Give me something fresh.NHe won't even try a bloody bullet catch.


00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:47.520
A bullet catch is suicide.


00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:51.590
All it takes is some smartassNvolunteer to put a button in the barrel.


00:13:51.660 --> 00:13:53.930
- Use a plant.N- You can't for every trick.


00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:55.970
No seats left for the punters.


00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:59.840
All right, no bullet catch, whatever,Nbut the point is a real magician


00:13:59.910 --> 00:14:01.530
tries to invent something new


00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:04.470
that other magicians willNscratch their heads over.


00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:06.740
Then you sell it to himNfor a small fortune.


00:14:06.810 --> 00:14:09.910
- What?N- I suppose you have such a trick?


00:14:09.980 --> 00:14:12.540
- I sure do.N- Would you care to sell it to me?


00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.210
No. No one else can do my trick.


00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:16.410
- Any trick can be duplicated.N- Wrong.


00:14:16.490 --> 00:14:20.220
If Mr. Borden has inventedNhis masterpiece,


00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:22.190
he's prepared to do it.


00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:24.390
Milton is a showman,Nbut Borden is right,


00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:26.090
he won't get his hands dirty.


00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:29.730
If you want to see whatNit takes to make real magic,


00:14:29.800 --> 00:14:33.640
go to the Tenley. There's a ChinamanNthere and he really has what it takes.


00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:35.940
- Chung Ling Soo.N- I can't afford that.


00:14:36.010 --> 00:14:37.740
I know the bloke run the door.


00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:42.140
You two go and see that show, andNwhichever one of you can tell me


00:14:42.210 --> 00:14:45.310
how he does the goldfish bowlNtrick gets the prize.


00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:47.650
- Which is?N- Ten minutes onstage


00:14:47.720 --> 00:14:49.550
with my old friend, Mr. Ackerman.


00:14:49.620 --> 00:14:51.050
- Really?N- Who's Ackerman?


00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:54.180
The top theatrical agent in London.


00:14:54.260 --> 00:14:57.250
- I saw you drop the knot again.N- I turned my wrists.


00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:59.960
Some nights youNjust don't get it, do you?


00:15:00.030 --> 00:15:02.900
I mean, if that knot slipsNand Julia's on the hoist,


00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:04.060
she'll break her leg.


00:15:04.140 --> 00:15:05.760
It's the wrong knot.


00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:08.710
Like I said, the LangfordNdouble will hold tighter.


00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:12.300
The Langford double isn'tNa wet knot. It's too dangerous.


00:15:12.380 --> 00:15:14.610
If the rope swells, she can't slip it.


00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:17.910
- I can slip a Langford underwater.N- We can practice.


00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:21.920
- Borden, he said no.N- Oh, you know knots better than me?


00:15:21.990 --> 00:15:23.980
Listen, no more mistakes.


00:15:24.060 --> 00:15:26.750
All right. Yeah? Do you?NYou want to take over?


00:15:26.830 --> 00:15:29.760
- Just leave.N- I didn't think so.


00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:36.030
Hey, Cutter, where's he from?


00:15:36.100 --> 00:15:39.400
Where are you from? He shiftsNprops for Virgil at the hall.


00:15:39.470 --> 00:15:42.630
- Worried he'll steal your tricks?N- Doesn't deal in methods.


00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:45.770
- How do you know?N- Because I hired him


00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:49.080
to find out how VirgilNdoes the orange trick.


00:15:49.150 --> 00:15:51.480
- I don't trust him.N- He's a natural magician.


00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:53.640
'Course you can't trust him.


00:15:53.720 --> 00:15:55.080
I think he's all right.


00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:57.490
- You think everyone's all right.N- Even you.


00:15:57.560 --> 00:16:01.390
Watch your sightlines. If I can see youNkiss your wife's leg every night,


00:16:01.460 --> 00:16:04.120
so can the blokes at the endsNof rows three and four!


00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:38.630
You're wrong. It can't be.


00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:42.430
- Look at the man.N- This is the trick.


00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:44.530
This is the performance. Right here.


00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:46.970
This is why no oneNcan detect his method.


00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:50.330
Total devotion to his art.


00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:53.070
A lot of self-sacrifice.


00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:55.510
You know.


00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:58.280
It's the only way to escape...


00:16:58.350 --> 00:17:00.780
...all this, you know?


00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:08.250
I can barely lift this thingNand it's not even filled with water.


00:17:09.900 --> 00:17:12.230
Or fish, look.


00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:14.560
I don't know. Hang on a second.


00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:19.200
He must be strong as an ox.


00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:24.670
He's been pretendingNto be a cripple for years.


00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:28.340
Any time he's in public,Nany time he goes out. It's unthinkable.


00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:31.350
Borden saw it at once.NBut I couldn't fathom it.


00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:34.280
Living my whole lifeNpretending to be someone else.


00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:36.080
You are pretending.


00:17:36.150 --> 00:17:38.180
I don't think changing a name compares.


00:17:38.260 --> 00:17:40.730
Not your name. Who you areNand where you're from.


00:17:40.790 --> 00:17:44.750
I promised I wouldn't embarrassNmy family with my theatrical endeavors.


00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:48.530
I thought of a name for you.


00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:53.390
The Great Danton.


00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:56.440
Do you like it? But it's sophisticated.


00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:57.940
It's French.


00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:08.080
Borden writes as if no one butNhe understood the true nature of magic.


00:18:13.730 --> 00:18:16.460
But what does he know of self-sacrifice?


00:18:21.570 --> 00:18:23.690
You bloody fool.


00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:54.860
- He killed it.N- It's OK.


00:18:54.930 --> 00:18:58.770
- He killed it.N- He didn't.


00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:04.540
Look, now he'll bring it back.


00:19:06.780 --> 00:19:09.710
- No, he killed it.N- No, he didn't.


00:19:18.020 --> 00:19:20.990
Look, see, he's all right. He's fine.


00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:25.160
- Look at him.N- But where's his brother?


00:19:27.870 --> 00:19:31.130
He's a sharp lad, your son.


00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:33.800
Oh, he's my nephew.


00:19:33.870 --> 00:19:35.360
Ah.


00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:41.100
You're the lucky one today.


00:20:01.700 --> 00:20:04.860
Are you watching closely?


00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:09.130
Look closer.


00:20:12.210 --> 00:20:14.010
Never show anyone.


00:20:14.080 --> 00:20:16.810
They'll beg youNand flatter you for the secret,


00:20:16.880 --> 00:20:20.370
but as soon as you give it up,Nyou'll be nothing to them.


00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:22.720
You understand? Nothing.


00:20:22.790 --> 00:20:25.850
The secret impresses no one.


00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:29.520
The trick you use it for is everything.


00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:36.700
Well, thank you for lunch, Mr. Borden.


00:20:36.770 --> 00:20:38.260
You're welcome.


00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:41.370
Alfred, it's Alfred.


00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:43.030
Alfred.


00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:46.080
So I could use a cup of tea.


00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:49.670
I can't allow...NIt's the landlord. It's not...


00:20:51.120 --> 00:20:54.350
You think that's...NIs that enough to keep me out?


00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:57.650
I think so.


00:20:58.660 --> 00:21:00.250
So I'll see you again?


00:21:09.470 --> 00:21:11.960
Milk and sugar?


00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:35.030
What's in there?


00:21:35.090 --> 00:21:37.030
Angier's machine.


00:21:45.600 --> 00:21:47.230
You built this, Mr. Cutter?


00:21:47.310 --> 00:21:50.170
Oh, no, sir. This wasn'tNbuilt by a magician.


00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:52.270
This was built by a wizard.


00:21:52.340 --> 00:21:57.340
A man who can actually doNwhat magicians pretend to do.


00:21:57.420 --> 00:22:01.610
Tell me, Your Honor, what happensNwith these things after the trial?


00:22:01.690 --> 00:22:03.650
They've been sold to a Lord Caldlow.


00:22:03.720 --> 00:22:06.490
An avid collector,Nvery interested in the case.


00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:09.050
Yeah. Well, don't let him take this.


00:22:09.130 --> 00:22:11.930
- Why ever not?N- It's too dangerous.


00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:14.160
I'm sure beneath its bells and whistles


00:22:14.230 --> 00:22:16.530
it's got a simpleNand disappointing trick.


00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:19.040
The most disappointing of all, sir.


00:22:21.210 --> 00:22:22.900
It has no trick.


00:22:25.340 --> 00:22:26.940
It's real.


00:22:30.050 --> 00:22:32.350
This is the tank Angier drowned in?


00:22:32.420 --> 00:22:34.480
Yes.


00:22:34.550 --> 00:22:36.710
This is the...


00:22:36.790 --> 00:22:39.850
...place where the performer'sNhand reaches through


00:22:39.930 --> 00:22:41.190
to the trick padlock.


00:22:41.260 --> 00:22:43.520
A standard magicalNapparatus for escapes?


00:22:43.600 --> 00:22:46.090
Yeah, with one important difference.


00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:48.190
This isn't a trick lock.


00:22:48.270 --> 00:22:50.230
It's been switched for a real one.


00:22:50.300 --> 00:22:52.270
What a way to kill someone.


00:22:52.340 --> 00:22:55.030
They're magicians, Your Honor.


00:22:55.110 --> 00:23:00.510
Showmen, men who live by dressing upNplain and sometimes brutal truths,


00:23:00.910 --> 00:23:03.680
to amaze, to shock.


00:23:03.750 --> 00:23:05.910
Even without an audience?


00:23:07.090 --> 00:23:09.050
There was an audience.


00:23:09.890 --> 00:23:11.950
You see, this water tank


00:23:12.020 --> 00:23:15.460
was of particular significanceNto these two men.


00:23:16.760 --> 00:23:19.290
Particularly awful significance.


00:23:22.200 --> 00:23:27.190
Which of you brave souls isNwilling to bind this lovely young woman?


00:23:29.770 --> 00:23:31.260
If you would tie her wrists,


00:23:31.340 --> 00:23:33.500
bind her feet around the ankle.


00:23:46.730 --> 00:23:49.320
- Are either of you gentlemen sailors?N- No.


00:23:51.300 --> 00:23:53.490
I'm sure you can both tie a strong knot.


00:24:48.690 --> 00:24:49.880
Robert!


00:25:12.040 --> 00:25:13.440
No, no.


00:25:17.420 --> 00:25:19.940
Julia. Julia!


00:26:04.630 --> 00:26:07.500
I knew an old sailor once.


00:26:07.570 --> 00:26:10.470
They told me he went overboard,


00:26:10.540 --> 00:26:12.630
tangled in the sails.


00:26:12.700 --> 00:26:14.500
They pulled him out,


00:26:14.570 --> 00:26:18.470
but it took him five minutes to cough.


00:26:18.540 --> 00:26:20.570
He said it was like...


00:26:20.650 --> 00:26:22.480
...going home.


00:26:27.820 --> 00:26:30.150
What do you want, Borden?


00:26:36.960 --> 00:26:38.990
I'm sorry for your loss, Angier.


00:26:42.800 --> 00:26:44.860
Which knot did you tie?


00:26:48.010 --> 00:26:50.940
I keep asking myself that.


00:26:51.010 --> 00:26:53.000
- And?N- And...


00:26:54.750 --> 00:26:57.610
I'm sorry, I just don't know.


00:26:59.680 --> 00:27:01.170
You don't know?


00:27:03.020 --> 00:27:04.960
I'm sorry.


00:27:05.920 --> 00:27:08.520
You don't know?


00:27:12.130 --> 00:27:14.330
You don't know?!


00:27:20.610 --> 00:27:23.940
- Alfred?N- Good news. We got our first booking.


00:27:24.410 --> 00:27:26.340
I don't think we've had the pleasure.


00:27:26.410 --> 00:27:29.440
- Mr. Fallon is my ingénieur.N- Where did you get all...?


00:27:29.510 --> 00:27:33.510
- I had to borrow and... don't ask.N- He's a very enterprising soul


00:27:33.590 --> 00:27:35.380
is... is Mr. Fallon. So...


00:27:35.450 --> 00:27:38.890
- We can't afford to pay him.N- The money will come with the audience.


00:27:38.960 --> 00:27:42.650
But what about until then?NWhat I earn, it's barely enough for us.


00:27:42.730 --> 00:27:46.690
Don't worry about it. I'll shareNhalf my food with him or something.


00:27:46.760 --> 00:27:49.730
You're going to beNdoing that with someone else.


00:27:49.800 --> 00:27:51.700
No. You're...


00:27:51.770 --> 00:27:54.030
Having a baby.


00:27:54.110 --> 00:27:57.010
Oh, my God.


00:27:57.080 --> 00:27:59.910
We should have told Fallon.NThat is great.


00:27:59.980 --> 00:28:02.450
Oh, come here.


00:28:02.510 --> 00:28:05.480
Oh.


00:28:05.550 --> 00:28:07.070
Alfred, what is this?


00:28:07.150 --> 00:28:11.320
Oh, this is just the trick to workNAckerman up at the end of my act.


00:28:11.390 --> 00:28:14.090
Is it the masterpiece, the great trick?


00:28:14.160 --> 00:28:16.920
No, no, no, the world isNnot ready for that one yet.


00:28:16.100 --> 00:28:21.330
This is just your run-of-the-mill,Ndaring, spectacular bullet catch.


00:28:21.400 --> 00:28:23.920
- A bullet catch.N- Yeah, but it's safe.


00:28:24.000 --> 00:28:26.300
I promise. Look.


00:28:28.670 --> 00:28:30.940
- Shoot me.N- Shoot you?


00:28:31.010 --> 00:28:32.240
Go on, shoot me.


00:28:34.750 --> 00:28:36.770
- Right there.N- No, I can't.


00:28:36.850 --> 00:28:39.410
No, no, not there.NShoot me here. Don't...


00:28:43.660 --> 00:28:46.520
How's that?


00:28:46.590 --> 00:28:49.920
That's very good. Tell me how you do it.


00:28:49.990 --> 00:28:51.120
No, I can't do that.


00:28:53.200 --> 00:28:56.060
- Well, then you can't do it.N- I can't do it?


00:28:56.130 --> 00:28:59.470
I'm sorry, but I can'tNraise a child on my own.


00:28:59.540 --> 00:29:01.870
You don't tell anybody that I told you.


00:29:01.940 --> 00:29:04.270
- OK.N- Gunpowder.


00:29:06.840 --> 00:29:07.970
Wadding.


00:29:09.610 --> 00:29:11.710
Then the bullet.


00:29:12.320 --> 00:29:14.050
Ramrod.


00:29:18.760 --> 00:29:20.750
Hold out your hand.


00:29:22.830 --> 00:29:26.760
The bullet is not even in theNgun when the charge is fired.


00:29:26.830 --> 00:29:30.600
Once you know,Nit's actually very obvious.


00:29:31.670 --> 00:29:33.660
Well, I mean, you still get...


00:29:33.740 --> 00:29:35.330
It's dangerous.


00:29:35.410 --> 00:29:37.600
- People still get killed doing that.N- How?


00:29:37.680 --> 00:29:40.410
You get some smartass whoNcould put a penny or a button


00:29:40.480 --> 00:29:43.810
or, God forbid, Sarah, somebodyNcould put a bullet down there.


00:29:43.880 --> 00:29:47.080
Don't worry. Don't worry,


00:29:47.150 --> 00:29:50.420
because I'm not gonna letNanything happen.


00:29:50.490 --> 00:29:53.360
Everything's gonnaNbe all right because...


00:29:54.730 --> 00:29:57.990
...I love you very much.


00:30:00.630 --> 00:30:03.930
- Say it again.N- I love you.


00:30:05.000 --> 00:30:07.470
- Not today.N- What?


00:30:07.540 --> 00:30:10.700
Well, some days it's not true,Nand today you don't mean it.


00:30:10.780 --> 00:30:14.010
Maybe today you're moreNin love with magic than me.


00:30:14.080 --> 00:30:16.710
I like being ableNto tell the difference.


00:30:16.780 --> 00:30:19.580
It makes the days it is true


00:30:19.650 --> 00:30:21.980
mean something.


00:30:23.620 --> 00:30:25.050
All right.


00:30:44.040 --> 00:30:47.340
Metal rings,Nladies and gentlemen.


00:30:47.410 --> 00:30:50.070
If there are anyNladies and gentlemen here.


00:30:50.150 --> 00:30:53.520
- Solid metal.N- Seen that already.


00:31:04.160 --> 00:31:05.250
Who threw that?


00:31:21.850 --> 00:31:23.640
This is what you came for, is it?


00:31:27.490 --> 00:31:28.980
So...


00:31:30.090 --> 00:31:31.990
...who wants to volunteer?


00:31:32.060 --> 00:31:33.820
- I do!N- Me!


00:31:41.570 --> 00:31:42.620
Me.


00:31:44.400 --> 00:31:46.460
Me.


00:31:59.880 --> 00:32:02.380
Are you man enough, sir?


00:32:07.360 --> 00:32:09.190
Yes.


00:32:19.970 --> 00:32:22.030
Which knot did you tie, Borden?


00:32:28.250 --> 00:32:30.510
Which knot did you tie, Borden?


00:32:31.680 --> 00:32:33.380
I don't know.


00:32:48.930 --> 00:32:52.600
He came in to demandNan answer, and I told him the truth.


00:32:52.670 --> 00:32:55.830
That I have fought with myselfNover that night,


00:32:55.910 --> 00:32:59.240
one half of me swearing blindNthat I tied a simple slipknot,


00:32:59.310 --> 00:33:02.680
the other half convincedNthat I tied the Langford double.


00:33:02.750 --> 00:33:04.770
I can never know for sure.


00:33:07.720 --> 00:33:09.980
How can he not know!


00:33:10.050 --> 00:33:11.820
How can he not know?


00:33:13.460 --> 00:33:15.950
He must know what he did.


00:33:16.030 --> 00:33:17.430
He must.


00:33:20.060 --> 00:33:22.060
Sarah, that bloody hurts.


00:33:22.770 --> 00:33:25.400
I don't understandNhow it can be bleeding again.


00:33:25.470 --> 00:33:27.900
It's as bad as the day it happened.


00:33:29.640 --> 00:33:33.580
- We have to get a doctor back.N- We can't afford the doctor back.


00:33:35.150 --> 00:33:38.740
- You've woken her.N- Great.


00:33:38.820 --> 00:33:41.720
I'm sorry, I need this to healNso I can get back to work.


00:33:41.790 --> 00:33:45.550
You've got to face things. What tricksNcan you perform with this injury?


00:33:45.620 --> 00:33:49.080
I can do car pulls.NI can do some prop tricks.


00:33:49.160 --> 00:33:53.530
I can still do that. I can doNthe trick I've been telling you about.


00:33:53.600 --> 00:33:55.730
The one that they'reNgonna remember me for.


00:33:58.100 --> 00:33:59.690
Come on.


00:34:25.260 --> 00:34:28.460
I never thought I'd find an answerNat the bottom of a pint glass.


00:34:28.530 --> 00:34:30.120
Hasn't stopped your looking.


00:34:35.340 --> 00:34:38.210
Heard about a booking.NNice little theater.


00:34:38.280 --> 00:34:41.110
- Young, up-and-coming magician.N- Who?


00:34:41.180 --> 00:34:43.910
- You.N- Me? Booking? Why?


00:34:43.980 --> 00:34:46.070
I want to keep on working.


00:34:46.150 --> 00:34:49.380
Who's going to hire the ingénieurNthat killed Julia McCullough


00:34:49.450 --> 00:34:51.580
in front of a sellout crowdNat the Orpheum?


00:34:52.360 --> 00:34:54.550
Someone who knows it wasn't your fault.


00:34:54.630 --> 00:34:58.120
Someone who knows Alfred BordenNand his repertoire of exotic knots.


00:34:58.200 --> 00:35:01.720
I hear he had a spot of bad luckNcatching a bullet south of the river.


00:35:01.800 --> 00:35:04.600
That's a dangerous trick, that one.


00:35:09.810 --> 00:35:11.780
We'll have to whitewash the windows,


00:35:11.840 --> 00:35:15.540
confound the more curiousNmembers of the public, but it will do.


00:35:17.380 --> 00:35:21.010
- We should see about an assistant.N- I've made some arrangements.


00:35:21.920 --> 00:35:23.680
You settled on a name?


00:35:24.590 --> 00:35:26.250
Yes, I have.


00:35:26.320 --> 00:35:28.190
The Great Danton.


00:35:28.260 --> 00:35:30.780
It's a bit old-fashioned, isn't it?


00:35:32.200 --> 00:35:34.430
No, it's sophisticated.


00:35:34.500 --> 00:35:37.260
The birdcage can't beNour climax. Everybody knows it.


00:35:37.340 --> 00:35:39.740
- Not like this.N- I don't want to kill doves.


00:35:39.800 --> 00:35:41.670
Then stay off the stage.


00:35:41.740 --> 00:35:43.430
You're a magician, not a wizard.


00:35:43.510 --> 00:35:47.380
You got to get your hands dirty, ifNyou're going to achieve the impossible.


00:35:48.850 --> 00:35:51.210
In here, Miss Wenscombe.


00:35:51.280 --> 00:35:55.740
No point in meeting Mr. AngierNif you don't fit. On the right.


00:35:58.920 --> 00:36:00.950
- What's so hard about this?N- Nothing.


00:36:01.030 --> 00:36:03.550
You're going... down here.


00:36:09.370 --> 00:36:12.230
- And this will conceal, right?N- Oh, sure.


00:36:12.900 --> 00:36:14.500
- Tighten up on there.N- Yep.


00:36:14.570 --> 00:36:15.600
OK.


00:36:17.710 --> 00:36:18.770
This ties up here?


00:36:18.840 --> 00:36:20.240
- Ties in the back.N- Good.


00:36:26.320 --> 00:36:28.510
Breathe as little as possible.


00:36:35.030 --> 00:36:37.650
Now, you see?


00:36:37.730 --> 00:36:39.130
- That's it.N- OK.


00:36:42.570 --> 00:36:44.400
She's not experienced,


00:36:44.470 --> 00:36:46.490
but she knows how to present herself.


00:36:46.570 --> 00:36:51.170
A pretty assistant is the mostNeffective form of misdirection.


00:36:51.240 --> 00:36:54.610
Thank you. Ladies and gentlemen,Nfor my final trick,


00:36:54.680 --> 00:36:57.440
I will require the assistanceNof two volunteers.


00:36:57.520 --> 00:36:59.780
Mr. Merrit, if you would oblige me?


00:37:01.690 --> 00:37:03.210
Yep.


00:37:05.020 --> 00:37:06.720
- Under?N- Under, yeah.


00:37:08.290 --> 00:37:09.590
Come around his foot.


00:37:09.660 --> 00:37:11.090
- Careful.N- It's all right.


00:37:31.950 --> 00:37:34.210
- Your volunteer, put their hand there.N- Yeah?


00:37:34.290 --> 00:37:36.120
And another one here.


00:37:36.190 --> 00:37:39.710
If you'll place your handsNon either side of the cage, please.


00:37:39.790 --> 00:37:41.120
Thank you, Olivia.


00:37:41.190 --> 00:37:44.960
You best not be intendingNto hurt this animal, Mr. Angier.


00:37:45.030 --> 00:37:47.400
- Of course not.N- Ready? Right.


00:37:48.170 --> 00:37:50.960
- One...N- Two...


00:37:51.700 --> 00:37:52.960
Three.


00:37:56.970 --> 00:37:58.770
That's bloody marvelous, Cutter.


00:37:59.780 --> 00:38:00.970
Very nice.


00:38:01.050 --> 00:38:02.840
And the best part is...


00:38:08.220 --> 00:38:10.650
I thought you said I hadNto get my hands dirty.


00:38:10.720 --> 00:38:12.620
Someday, perhaps you will.


00:38:12.690 --> 00:38:14.250
I just had to know that you can.


00:38:14.330 --> 00:38:16.260
Very nice. Very nice, indeed.


00:38:16.330 --> 00:38:19.990
I haven't had the chance to complimentNyou on your beautiful theater.


00:38:20.060 --> 00:38:22.430
It'll be a lot moreNbeautiful when it's full.


00:38:22.500 --> 00:38:23.490
Don't worry.


00:38:23.570 --> 00:38:25.800
You all say that. Why should I worry?


00:38:25.870 --> 00:38:28.740
If your tricks don't get themNin, somebody else's will.


00:38:28.810 --> 00:38:32.900
Maybe somebody willingNto do a bullet catch or a water escape?


00:38:32.980 --> 00:38:34.540
Cheap thrills, Mr. Merrit.


00:38:34.610 --> 00:38:38.280
People hoping for an accident,Nlikely to see one too.


00:38:38.350 --> 00:38:40.340
What would that do for your business?


00:38:40.420 --> 00:38:43.280
You got a week, John.


00:38:43.350 --> 00:38:46.720
Thank you, Mr. Merrit.


00:38:54.700 --> 00:38:56.060
Thank you.


00:38:57.870 --> 00:39:01.500
Uh... Sir, in the third row there.


00:39:01.570 --> 00:39:04.270
Please stand upNand show us your handkerchief.


00:39:06.280 --> 00:39:08.070
This isn't mine.


00:39:08.150 --> 00:39:11.600
Perhaps you'd return it to the ladyNin the aisle of the second row.


00:39:11.680 --> 00:39:13.980
I believe she has yours.


00:39:20.320 --> 00:39:24.990
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry. I'm makingNso many mistakes. I'm so nervous.


00:39:25.060 --> 00:39:27.330
The audience doesn't seemNto be responding.


00:39:27.400 --> 00:39:29.630
They've seen a lot of tricks before,


00:39:29.700 --> 00:39:32.190
but not this next one.


00:39:41.250 --> 00:39:43.010
Cloth over.


00:39:43.080 --> 00:39:44.840
Keep your fingers crossed.


00:39:44.920 --> 00:39:47.180
I'll have the champagne ready.


00:40:01.670 --> 00:40:04.960
- You've seen this one before?N- We've seen them all before.


00:40:05.040 --> 00:40:07.160
I'll make it a littleNharder then, shall I?


00:40:07.240 --> 00:40:10.210
Two volunteers, please.NA lady and a gentlemen.


00:40:10.270 --> 00:40:13.470
To hold this cage with me.


00:40:13.540 --> 00:40:15.510
I'll perform this feat in a manner


00:40:15.580 --> 00:40:20.110
never before seen by yourselves or anyNother audience anywhere in the world.


00:40:22.590 --> 00:40:25.210
Madame, place one handNon the back of the cage,


00:40:25.290 --> 00:40:26.810
one hand on the front.


00:40:26.890 --> 00:40:29.260
Sir, one hand on the bottom of the cage


00:40:29.330 --> 00:40:30.850
one hand on the top.


00:40:44.200 --> 00:40:47.100
- I should've spotted him.N- You had a lot of plates going.


00:40:47.170 --> 00:40:49.330
- Don't suppose we can do this again.N- No.


00:40:49.410 --> 00:40:51.840
- So, what's the climax of our show?N- Show?


00:40:51.910 --> 00:40:55.040
- You don't have a show.N- We have a week's engagement.


00:40:55.110 --> 00:40:58.710
To perform magic, not butcher birdsNand break my customers' fingers.


00:40:58.780 --> 00:41:01.480
Clear out, anything hereNin the morning gets burned.


00:41:01.550 --> 00:41:03.990
- Mr. Merrit...N- It's done, John.


00:41:04.060 --> 00:41:06.850
I've hired a comedian.NYou know I hate comedians.


00:41:08.990 --> 00:41:11.480
Well, there'sNplenty of good theaters.


00:41:11.560 --> 00:41:14.400
If we can come up with a new trick,


00:41:14.470 --> 00:41:17.700
- change the name of the act.N- The name stays.


00:41:19.540 --> 00:41:24.670
Right, well, then the new trick'sNgonna have to be irresistible then.


00:41:24.740 --> 00:41:26.770
I have a couple of methods to try out.


00:41:26.850 --> 00:41:30.080
And then we need a new angleNon the presentation.


00:41:30.150 --> 00:41:31.980
And if you need some inspiration,


00:41:32.050 --> 00:41:35.210
there's a technical expositionNat the Albert Hall this week.


00:41:35.290 --> 00:41:38.020
Engineers, scientists, you know?


00:41:38.090 --> 00:41:41.390
That sort of thing capturesNthe public's imagination.


00:41:58.440 --> 00:42:01.840
Mind if I join you? Tesla sendsNme down here during the storms.


00:42:01.910 --> 00:42:05.140
Perfect excuse to come joinNthe Great Danton for a drink.


00:42:06.120 --> 00:42:08.520
Two of them.


00:42:08.590 --> 00:42:11.210
Beautiful, isn't it?NGod, I miss New York, though.


00:42:11.290 --> 00:42:13.720
- Why are you here?N- The lightning lives here.


00:42:13.790 --> 00:42:15.420
And not much else.


00:42:15.490 --> 00:42:17.020
Our work is secret.


00:42:17.660 --> 00:42:19.560
That a cipher?


00:42:21.670 --> 00:42:24.790
A rotating transpositionNthat shifts every day of the diary.


00:42:24.870 --> 00:42:28.860
Simple but time-consuming to translate,Neven with the five-letter keyword.


00:42:28.940 --> 00:42:30.670
Which is?


00:42:30.740 --> 00:42:32.730
We magicians have a circle of trust.


00:42:32.810 --> 00:42:36.910
You have a circle of trustNwith someone whose diary you stole?


00:42:36.980 --> 00:42:38.740
Maybe I bought it.


00:42:38.820 --> 00:42:41.550
And you're hoping to findNa great secret in there?


00:42:41.620 --> 00:42:43.920
I've already found it.


00:42:43.990 --> 00:42:45.390
That's why I'm here.


00:42:51.600 --> 00:42:54.220
Tesla built one for another magician.


00:42:54.300 --> 00:42:56.060
Why would you want the same thing?


00:42:56.130 --> 00:42:58.130
Call it a professional rivalry.


00:42:58.200 --> 00:43:02.330
Mr. Tesla has built unusualNmachines for unusual people.


00:43:03.340 --> 00:43:06.440
- But he would never talk about it.N- I understand discretion.


00:43:06.510 --> 00:43:07.810
I just want the machine.


00:43:11.150 --> 00:43:12.810
Finish your drink.


00:43:13.790 --> 00:43:16.480
I want to show you something.NI think you'll have


00:43:16.550 --> 00:43:18.780
a special appreciation for our work.


00:43:18.860 --> 00:43:22.320
- I thought it was a secret.N- You're a magician.


00:43:22.390 --> 00:43:24.120
Who's gonna believe you?


00:43:25.300 --> 00:43:27.490
Not long now.


00:43:27.570 --> 00:43:30.030
Our equipment requiresNa great deal of current.


00:43:30.100 --> 00:43:31.830
Tesla electrified the whole town


00:43:31.900 --> 00:43:34.960
in exchange for using theNgenerators when we need them.


00:43:36.170 --> 00:43:39.370
We do our tests whenNthe townspeople are asleep.


00:43:39.440 --> 00:43:42.140
Mr. Tesla doesn't wantNto scare anyone.


00:43:59.960 --> 00:44:01.990
Where are the wires?


00:44:03.370 --> 00:44:04.630
Exactly.


00:44:13.850 --> 00:44:16.540
Where's the generator?


00:44:16.610 --> 00:44:18.050
You saw it last week.


00:44:18.120 --> 00:44:21.210
- That must be ten miles from here.N- Fifteen.


00:44:21.290 --> 00:44:25.380
And I have to ride all of themNbefore I get to bed.


00:44:25.460 --> 00:44:28.150
I'll send word for youNin a few days, Mr. Angier.


00:44:28.230 --> 00:44:32.320
Magic. Real magic.


00:44:32.400 --> 00:44:34.520
Now appearing, only hereNat London's Royal Albert Hall,


00:44:36.570 --> 00:44:38.870
one of the miracles of our age.


00:44:38.940 --> 00:44:43.530
A technological marvel. You've neverNseen anything like it in your lives.


00:44:43.610 --> 00:44:46.340
Your eyes will not believeNwhat they're witnessing.


00:44:46.410 --> 00:44:49.280
The miracle of Nikola Tesla,Nladies and gentlemen.


00:44:49.350 --> 00:44:51.840
Free, clean power.NLike to know the future?


00:44:51.920 --> 00:44:54.980
The man who's speaking right nowNis going to change the world.


00:44:55.050 --> 00:44:59.420
Come one, come all.NImmediate seating, no waiting.


00:45:14.540 --> 00:45:15.770
Ladies and gentlemen,


00:45:17.880 --> 00:45:19.710
objections have been raised...


00:45:19.780 --> 00:45:23.210
They should be raised.NDoes that look safe to you?


00:45:23.280 --> 00:45:25.840
Part of Thomas Edison's smear campaign


00:45:25.920 --> 00:45:31.620
against Mr. Tesla'sNsuperior alternating current.


00:45:31.690 --> 00:45:34.520
We have asked Mr. TeslaNto reconsider.


00:45:34.590 --> 00:45:37.080
Which he will not!


00:45:37.160 --> 00:45:42.330
But I've been told he refusesNto appear under any such restrictions.


00:45:42.400 --> 00:45:44.960
This thing's gonna blow.


00:45:46.300 --> 00:45:48.740
Ladies and gentlemen, please.


00:46:27.450 --> 00:46:28.570
Hey.


00:46:30.820 --> 00:46:33.250
Hello, Jess.


00:46:35.720 --> 00:46:39.520
Have you had a nice dayNwith mommy? Huh?


00:46:40.460 --> 00:46:42.480
Sarah.


00:46:42.560 --> 00:46:45.460
- I love you.N- See, today it's true.


00:46:45.530 --> 00:46:48.090
- Yeah.N- Hello.


00:46:50.000 --> 00:46:52.370
I saw happiness.


00:46:52.440 --> 00:46:55.070
Happiness that should have been mine.


00:46:55.140 --> 00:46:57.160
But I was wrong.


00:46:57.240 --> 00:47:01.870
His notebook reveals thatNhe never had the life that I envied.


00:47:01.950 --> 00:47:04.570
The family lifeNthat he craves one minute,


00:47:04.650 --> 00:47:08.950
he rails against the next,Ndemanding freedom.


00:47:09.020 --> 00:47:12.010
His mind... his mind is a divided one.


00:47:12.090 --> 00:47:13.520
His soul is restless.


00:47:13.590 --> 00:47:15.720
His wife and child, tormented


00:47:15.790 --> 00:47:19.750
by his fickle and contradictory nature.


00:47:23.970 --> 00:47:26.460
So, what do you think you'll call her?


00:47:26.540 --> 00:47:27.900
I don't know.


00:47:27.970 --> 00:47:30.270
Everybody needs a name, so, what's hers?


00:47:31.180 --> 00:47:32.970
Maybe Sarah.


00:47:35.350 --> 00:47:37.750
That's a lovely name.NThat's a lovely name.


00:47:37.820 --> 00:47:41.050
Well, you talk about what you wantNto do for the rest of the day.


00:47:41.120 --> 00:47:42.980
All right, go on, you talk with her.


00:47:45.420 --> 00:47:49.690
Are they taking her away?


00:47:49.760 --> 00:47:51.660
To the workhouse?


00:47:54.500 --> 00:47:55.990
You keep talking.


00:47:58.700 --> 00:48:01.100
Tell Owens I've reconsidered. Take it.


00:48:01.170 --> 00:48:02.970
Go on, take it.


00:48:06.540 --> 00:48:08.670
It's for the best.


00:48:13.480 --> 00:48:16.080
Let me see.


00:48:16.150 --> 00:48:18.780
I'm gonna learnNall the professor's secrets.


00:48:18.860 --> 00:48:22.290
Only if I teach you how to read.


00:48:22.360 --> 00:48:24.730
They're just stupid tricks, right?


00:48:24.800 --> 00:48:28.030
Haven't helped youNget out of here, have they?


00:48:28.100 --> 00:48:31.430
Or can't you undo real locks, professor?


00:48:32.800 --> 00:48:35.470
Maybe I'm just biding my time.


00:48:35.540 --> 00:48:38.030
Maybe one day I'll...


00:48:38.110 --> 00:48:40.740
...open my hand, get your attention,


00:48:40.810 --> 00:48:43.710
ask, "Are you watching closely?"


00:48:43.780 --> 00:48:45.870
Maybe a magic whirl or two.


00:48:48.490 --> 00:48:50.320
And then I'll be gone.


00:48:53.930 --> 00:48:56.990
How'd you get so famous then?


00:48:57.900 --> 00:48:59.620
Magic.


00:49:02.100 --> 00:49:04.970
Oi! Borden, get back here!


00:49:05.040 --> 00:49:06.590
Thank you.


00:49:06.670 --> 00:49:08.640
Shut up!


00:49:11.940 --> 00:49:14.040
Where's the bloody key?!


00:49:20.650 --> 00:49:23.120
February 8,1899.


00:49:23.190 --> 00:49:25.310
Today, finally, a breakthrough.


00:49:25.390 --> 00:49:28.120
Tesla's agreed to see me.


00:49:35.870 --> 00:49:37.030
Perfectly safe.


00:49:58.560 --> 00:50:02.320
So this is the Great Danton.


00:50:02.390 --> 00:50:06.990
Mr. Alley has effused about your actNto me on any number of occasions.


00:50:08.830 --> 00:50:10.390
Hold out other hand.


00:50:18.980 --> 00:50:22.780
- What's conducting the electricity?N- Our bodies, Mr. Angier.


00:50:22.850 --> 00:50:27.050
Quite capable of conductingNand, indeed, producing energy.


00:50:28.590 --> 00:50:30.650
Have you eaten, Mr. Angier?


00:50:32.560 --> 00:50:35.720
I need something impossible.


00:50:37.500 --> 00:50:42.260
You're familiar with the phrase,N"Man's reach exceeds his grasp"?


00:50:42.330 --> 00:50:44.030
Is a lie.


00:50:44.100 --> 00:50:46.130
Man's grasp exceeds his nerve.


00:50:47.340 --> 00:50:50.210
Society only toleratesNone change at a time.


00:50:51.680 --> 00:50:54.940
First time I tried to change the world,


00:50:55.010 --> 00:50:56.780
I was hailed as a visionary.


00:50:57.280 --> 00:50:59.410
Second time...


00:50:59.480 --> 00:51:02.510
...I was asked politely to retire.


00:51:03.650 --> 00:51:07.180
So here I am, enjoying my retirement.


00:51:07.260 --> 00:51:11.130
Nothing is impossible, Mr. Angier.NWhat you want is simply expensive.


00:51:11.200 --> 00:51:13.430
If I were to build for you this machine,


00:51:13.500 --> 00:51:16.560
you would be presenting itNmerely as illusion?


00:51:16.630 --> 00:51:19.970
Well, if people actuallyNbelieved the things I did on stage,


00:51:20.040 --> 00:51:22.440
they wouldn't clap, they'd scream.


00:51:22.510 --> 00:51:24.500
Think of sawing a woman in half.


00:51:24.580 --> 00:51:26.910
Have you considered the cost of this?


00:51:26.980 --> 00:51:28.910
Price is not an object.


00:51:28.980 --> 00:51:32.940
Perhaps not, but have youNconsidered the cost?


00:51:33.920 --> 00:51:35.250
I'm not sure I follow.


00:51:36.320 --> 00:51:38.150
Go home, forget this thing.


00:51:38.220 --> 00:51:40.420
I can recognize an obsession.


00:51:40.490 --> 00:51:44.520
- No good will come of it.N- Hasn't good come of your obsessions?


00:51:44.600 --> 00:51:47.830
At first, but I haveNfollowed them too long.


00:51:47.900 --> 00:51:49.830
I am their slave.


00:51:49.900 --> 00:51:52.990
And one day,Nthey will choose to destroy me.


00:51:54.810 --> 00:51:59.240
If you understand an obsession, thenNyou know you won't change my mind.


00:52:00.180 --> 00:52:01.170
So be it.


00:52:02.680 --> 00:52:04.010
Will you build it?


00:52:04.980 --> 00:52:08.540
I've already begunNto build it, Mr. Angier.


00:52:08.620 --> 00:52:12.610
I hope you enjoy the mountain air.NThis will take some time.


00:52:36.550 --> 00:52:39.240
Uh... I thought you'd gone.


00:52:40.380 --> 00:52:42.850
I don't really have anywhere to go.


00:52:44.820 --> 00:52:46.720
You've been sleeping here?


00:52:46.790 --> 00:52:51.520
Cutter said it'd be all right till weNget another booking. What are you doing?


00:52:51.600 --> 00:52:53.830
Uh... research.


00:52:53.900 --> 00:52:55.330
Part of a magician's job


00:52:55.400 --> 00:52:58.270
is to... watch his competition,Nsee what illusions...


00:52:58.340 --> 00:53:01.270
You're going to do somethingNto that man, aren't you?


00:53:01.340 --> 00:53:03.200
Cutter's hoping you let things lie.


00:53:03.270 --> 00:53:06.140
He says if Borden thinksNthings are even between you...


00:53:06.210 --> 00:53:08.040
Even?


00:53:08.110 --> 00:53:10.670
My wife for a couple of his fingers?


00:53:10.750 --> 00:53:13.840
He has a family nowNand he's performing again.


00:53:13.920 --> 00:53:16.750
Borden is out there livingNhis life just as he intended,


00:53:16.820 --> 00:53:19.520
as if nothing had happenedNand look at me.


00:53:19.590 --> 00:53:22.080
I'm alone and no theater will touch me.


00:53:22.160 --> 00:53:23.750
Us.


00:53:23.830 --> 00:53:26.190
You're going to need a better disguise.


00:53:43.710 --> 00:53:45.910
I need a volunteer.


00:53:45.980 --> 00:53:47.450
What happened?


00:53:48.450 --> 00:53:50.280
Did you hurt him?


00:53:52.190 --> 00:53:53.490
What happened, Robert?


00:53:55.890 --> 00:53:59.850
You, sir. Just a rubber ball, yes?


00:53:59.930 --> 00:54:01.020
Thank you.


00:54:01.100 --> 00:54:03.690
Just a rubber ball? No.


00:54:03.770 --> 00:54:06.960
Not normal. Not a normal rubber ball.


00:54:07.040 --> 00:54:08.160
It's magic.


00:54:08.970 --> 00:54:11.030
He had a new trick.


00:54:25.060 --> 00:54:26.610
Was it good?


00:54:30.100 --> 00:54:34.950
It was the greatestNmagic trick I've ever seen.


00:54:38.870 --> 00:54:40.100
Did they applaudNwhen you saw it?


00:54:41.070 --> 00:54:44.940
It was too good. It was too simple.NThe audience hardly had time to see it.


00:54:45.010 --> 00:54:47.880
- He's a dreadful magician.N- A wonderful magician.


00:54:47.950 --> 00:54:50.470
He's a dreadful showman.NHe doesn't dress it up,


00:54:50.550 --> 00:54:52.380
- how to sell it.N- How does he do it?


00:54:52.450 --> 00:54:54.470
- He uses a double.N- No, it's too simple.


00:54:54.550 --> 00:54:56.040
This is a complex illusion.


00:54:56.120 --> 00:54:58.520
You say that becauseNyou don't know the method.


00:54:58.590 --> 00:55:00.990
It's a double that comes out.NIt's the only way.


00:55:01.060 --> 00:55:04.960
I've seen him perform it three times.NThe prestige is the same man.


00:55:05.030 --> 00:55:08.560
- No, it's not.N- The same man comes out of the cabinet.


00:55:08.630 --> 00:55:10.900
It's the same man.


00:55:10.970 --> 00:55:13.660
He wears padded glovesNto hide his damaged fingers,


00:55:13.740 --> 00:55:16.330
but, if you look closely, you can tell.


00:55:18.040 --> 00:55:20.910
He doesn't know how to sell itNto an audience, but I do.


00:55:20.980 --> 00:55:23.410
Yeah, we could use itNas a climax to the show.


00:55:23.480 --> 00:55:25.880
Yes.


00:55:25.950 --> 00:55:29.150
The man stole my life,NI'm gonna steal his trick.


00:55:29.220 --> 00:55:31.380
We got to find someoneNwho looks like you.


00:55:31.460 --> 00:55:34.980
- He doesn't use a double.N- I don't know how Borden does it.


00:55:35.060 --> 00:55:39.550
Either... You either wait for himNto retire and buy the secret,


00:55:39.630 --> 00:55:41.430
or you listen to how I would do it.


00:55:41.500 --> 00:55:44.020
And the only wayNthat I know how to do it


00:55:44.100 --> 00:55:46.570
is to find you a bloody good double.


00:55:47.570 --> 00:55:48.970
All right.


00:55:50.410 --> 00:55:52.900
Take a good look.NLet's get out there and find me.


00:55:52.980 --> 00:55:55.100
Whoo!


00:55:55.180 --> 00:55:56.670
Look, look.


00:56:01.220 --> 00:56:02.740
What's that?


00:56:06.090 --> 00:56:08.390
- It's for you.N- What's this for?


00:56:09.030 --> 00:56:10.860
Come.


00:56:13.100 --> 00:56:15.760
You...


00:56:15.830 --> 00:56:19.860
- I asked you last week...N- You caught me in a wrong mood.


00:56:19.940 --> 00:56:22.130
- But you won't ever...N- Sarah,


00:56:22.210 --> 00:56:25.370
I'm gonna haveNto change my mind, aren't I?


00:56:25.440 --> 00:56:30.110
The act is taking off. Soon we'll be inNa bigger theater, things will work out.


00:56:32.680 --> 00:56:36.480
I can't believe it. Thank you.NThank you. It's beautiful.


00:56:43.130 --> 00:56:46.220
- Gerry?N- Darling, look at you.


00:56:46.300 --> 00:56:49.270
Mr. Cutter, Mr. Angier,NI'd like you to meet Gerald Root.


00:56:49.330 --> 00:56:51.490
Mm-hm.


00:56:54.340 --> 00:56:58.270
A pleasure. PleasureNto meet you fine gentlemen.


00:56:58.340 --> 00:57:02.070
Would you like for meNto tell you a little joke? Come here.


00:57:05.120 --> 00:57:08.210
Yes. Are you laughing now?


00:57:11.660 --> 00:57:13.280
I have to take a piss.


00:57:14.690 --> 00:57:17.790
- He's out of his mind.N- Of course, he's an out-of-work actor.


00:57:17.860 --> 00:57:19.760
He's perfect. He needs a little help.


00:57:19.830 --> 00:57:22.800
But when I get done with him,Nhe could be your brother.


00:57:22.870 --> 00:57:25.460
I don't need him to be myNbrother, I need him to be me.


00:57:25.540 --> 00:57:27.230
Give me a month.


00:57:34.010 --> 00:57:36.640
So you open the door...


00:57:36.710 --> 00:57:38.180
...and...


00:57:45.560 --> 00:57:47.320
Come on.


00:57:51.030 --> 00:57:52.960
Couldn't you have found a softer one?


00:57:53.030 --> 00:57:55.360
Well, it's not for sleeping on.


00:57:55.430 --> 00:57:57.490
So, if you come down through there...


00:58:00.170 --> 00:58:03.200
- ...does Root go up through there?N- Yep.


00:58:03.270 --> 00:58:05.330
It's going to be amazing.


00:58:05.410 --> 00:58:08.870
Well, it has to be. Borden'sNtrick is getting noticed.


00:58:11.720 --> 00:58:14.080
The place was packed today.


00:58:15.690 --> 00:58:17.480
You went and saw his show again.


00:58:17.550 --> 00:58:19.990
Ready to meet yourself, Mr. Angier?


00:58:28.370 --> 00:58:30.700
All I have to do isNkeep myself stinking drunk,


00:58:30.770 --> 00:58:33.100
and no one will be ableNto tell the difference.


00:58:33.170 --> 00:58:35.260
Have a little faith, sir.


00:58:35.340 --> 00:58:39.240
Now, would you favor usNwith a performance, Mr. Root?


00:58:59.100 --> 00:59:04.160
You'd drink, too, if you knewNthe world half as well as I do.


00:59:07.870 --> 00:59:09.570
Did you think you were unique?


00:59:09.640 --> 00:59:12.340
I've been Caesar, I've played Faust.


00:59:12.410 --> 00:59:15.500
How difficult could it possiblyNbe to play the Great Danton?


00:59:15.580 --> 00:59:18.710
You can go back to beingNyourself now, Root, for nothing.


00:59:18.780 --> 00:59:21.050
I'd rather be him for now.


00:59:21.120 --> 00:59:23.880
I find it, uh... amusing.


00:59:27.320 --> 00:59:29.050
"My liege,


00:59:29.130 --> 00:59:32.460
I did deny no prisoners."


00:59:32.530 --> 00:59:34.690
- You look wonderful.N- Oh, thank you.


00:59:34.770 --> 00:59:38.030
Root has to keep a low profile.NAnyone sees him, the game's up.


00:59:38.100 --> 00:59:40.900
I don't know how you do things.NI'm not sure I wanna know.


00:59:40.970 --> 00:59:43.300
Have you thought what we should call it?


00:59:43.370 --> 00:59:47.540
There's no point being coy. BordenNcalls his trick The Transported Man.


00:59:51.450 --> 00:59:54.610
Ladies and gentlemen, muchNof what you've seen may be termed


00:59:54.690 --> 00:59:58.450
as illusions or entertaining trifles.


01:00:03.130 --> 01:00:04.180
Alas...


01:00:06.360 --> 01:00:08.890
...I cannot claimNthis next feat as illusion.


01:00:09.800 --> 01:00:10.990
Watch carefully.


01:00:12.440 --> 01:00:14.870
You will see no trickery,


01:00:14.940 --> 01:00:18.030
for no trickery is employed.


01:00:18.110 --> 01:00:21.480
Merely a technique familiarNto certain citizens of the Orient


01:00:21.550 --> 01:00:23.710
and various holy men of the Himalayas.


01:00:26.980 --> 01:00:30.010
Indeed, many of you may beNfamiliar with this technique,


01:00:30.090 --> 01:00:33.250
but for those of you whoNare not, do not be alarmed.


01:00:33.320 --> 01:00:36.380
What you're about to seeNis considered safe.


01:01:07.960 --> 01:01:11.020
To our achievement.


01:01:11.090 --> 01:01:13.860
The manager says he'sNnever seen a reaction like it.


01:01:13.930 --> 01:01:17.230
At least he saw it. I spentNthe ovation hiding under the stage.


01:01:17.300 --> 01:01:19.630
No one cares aboutNthe man who disappears.


01:01:19.700 --> 01:01:21.690
They care about the one who comes out.


01:01:21.770 --> 01:01:23.830
I care about the man in the box.


01:01:23.910 --> 01:01:28.210
Thank you. I don't know,Nmaybe we could switch before the trick.


01:01:28.280 --> 01:01:30.440
I'm the prestige,Nand Root's below stage.


01:01:30.510 --> 01:01:33.450
No, the anticipationNof the trick is everything.


01:01:33.520 --> 01:01:36.580
We need your showmanshipNto build up the suspense.


01:01:36.650 --> 01:01:40.210
Once Root opens his mouth, it's over.NHe can't introduce this trick.


01:01:40.290 --> 01:01:43.020
Of course I can. I'm the Great Danton.


01:01:43.090 --> 01:01:46.690
Root, you bloody fool,Nget out of that wardrobe and makeup.


01:01:46.760 --> 01:01:49.430
Anyone could walk in here at any minute.


01:01:49.500 --> 01:01:51.560
Congratulations, all.


01:01:51.640 --> 01:01:55.330
Life is not full of theseNmoments. We worked hard.


01:01:55.410 --> 01:01:57.070
We need to celebrate properly.


01:02:00.810 --> 01:02:03.280
What's wrong? Is it your wife?


01:02:03.350 --> 01:02:05.650
No, it's the trick.NIt isn't good enough.


01:02:05.720 --> 01:02:09.050
Borden's trick is nothingNcompared to ours. He has no style.


01:02:09.120 --> 01:02:12.990
He doesn't spend the finaleNhiding under the stage.


01:02:13.060 --> 01:02:15.960
- I need to know how he does it.N- Why?


01:02:16.030 --> 01:02:18.520
So I can do it better.


01:02:20.600 --> 01:02:23.070
I need you to go and work for him.


01:02:26.100 --> 01:02:27.830
Work for him? Are you joking?


01:02:29.110 --> 01:02:30.300
You'll be my spy.


01:02:30.370 --> 01:02:32.570
We just got our start.NYou want me to leave?


01:02:32.640 --> 01:02:34.740
That's how we advance. Think of it.


01:02:34.810 --> 01:02:38.010
People are excited by Cutter'sNversion. Imagine what we'd do


01:02:38.080 --> 01:02:42.520
with the real illusion. We'd have theNgreatest magic act anyone's ever seen.


01:02:42.590 --> 01:02:46.350
- He knows I work for you.N- Exactly why he'll want to hire you.


01:02:46.420 --> 01:02:48.980
- He'll want my secret.N- Why would he trust me?


01:02:49.060 --> 01:02:51.760
Because you'reNgonna tell him the truth.


01:02:54.670 --> 01:02:56.500
Hmm?


01:03:04.040 --> 01:03:05.170
Good girl.


01:03:08.350 --> 01:03:11.870
You must be curious to see whatNso much money has bought you.


01:03:12.550 --> 01:03:15.450
Fitting you should be hereNfor her maiden voyage.


01:03:15.520 --> 01:03:17.350
Your hat.


01:03:25.300 --> 01:03:27.890
You might want to stand back.


01:03:48.350 --> 01:03:49.480
I don't understand.


01:03:49.550 --> 01:03:51.890
Perhaps it would be bestNif you left us to it.


01:03:51.960 --> 01:03:53.580
Is there a problem, Mr. Tesla?


01:03:53.660 --> 01:03:55.680
- No. Come back next week.N- Next week?


01:03:55.760 --> 01:03:58.320
- Next week, it will be fine.N- Tesla!


01:03:58.400 --> 01:04:00.120
Just a little temperamental.


01:04:05.970 --> 01:04:08.870
- Interesting workshop.N- Yeah, we make do.


01:04:08.940 --> 01:04:11.100
- My name is Olivia...N- I know who you are.


01:04:11.170 --> 01:04:12.840
Here to steal the rest of my show?


01:04:12.910 --> 01:04:14.810
To give your show what it's missing.


01:04:14.880 --> 01:04:18.110
- Yeah, what might that be?N- Me.


01:04:18.180 --> 01:04:22.640
I was justNsaying that, wasn't I?


01:04:22.720 --> 01:04:25.020
- A woman's touch.N- I've left Angier.


01:04:25.090 --> 01:04:27.150
- All right.N- I want a job.


01:04:27.220 --> 01:04:28.560
Yeah.


01:04:28.630 --> 01:04:30.460
I know you've no reason to trust me.


01:04:30.530 --> 01:04:32.090
Why wouldn't I trust you?


01:04:32.160 --> 01:04:35.600
You're only the mistress of myNenemy. Why wouldn't I trust you?


01:04:37.270 --> 01:04:39.200
- Mr. Borden.N- Alfred.


01:04:41.640 --> 01:04:43.300
I'm going to tell you the truth.


01:04:43.370 --> 01:04:45.600
Now that is a slippery notion


01:04:45.680 --> 01:04:48.010
in our line of work,Nisn't it, Miss Wenscombe?


01:04:50.110 --> 01:04:52.780
I am here because he sent me here.


01:04:52.850 --> 01:04:55.320
He wants me to work for youNand steal your secret.


01:04:55.390 --> 01:04:58.750
What does he need my secret for?NHis trick is topnotch.


01:04:58.820 --> 01:05:01.420
He vanishes,Nand then he reappears instantly


01:05:01.490 --> 01:05:03.980
on the other sideNof the stage, mute, overweight


01:05:04.060 --> 01:05:06.620
and, unless I'm mistaken, very drunk.


01:05:06.700 --> 01:05:10.190
It's astonishing. How doesNhe do it? And tell me, Olivia,


01:05:10.270 --> 01:05:13.730
does he enjoy taking his bowsNunder the stage?


01:05:13.800 --> 01:05:17.100
It's killing him. He's obsessedNwith discovering your methods.


01:05:17.170 --> 01:05:20.230
He thinks of nothing else,Ntakes no pleasure in our success.


01:05:20.310 --> 01:05:21.800
And I've had enough.


01:05:21.880 --> 01:05:24.280
There is no future with him.


01:05:25.420 --> 01:05:29.150
He sent me here to steal your secrets,Nbut I've come to offer you his.


01:05:29.220 --> 01:05:33.120
This is the truth... is it?


01:05:37.660 --> 01:05:39.960
Think you'd better get dressed, sir.


01:05:40.030 --> 01:05:44.060
Root, you're late and more drunk thanNusual. Get down below stairs right away.


01:05:44.130 --> 01:05:45.860
No.


01:05:45.940 --> 01:05:49.300
No, we need to haveNa little chat, Mr. Cutter.


01:05:49.370 --> 01:05:53.710
We have a problem. Cutter, BordenNis performing right across the street.


01:05:53.780 --> 01:05:57.040
Yeah, we have a bigger problem.


01:05:57.110 --> 01:06:00.110
Root. He's realizedNthat he can make demands.


01:06:00.180 --> 01:06:02.280
Wha...? He's blackmailing us?


01:06:02.350 --> 01:06:04.320
I was surprised, to tell you the truth.


01:06:04.390 --> 01:06:06.980
It usually takes themNa lot longer to figure it out.


01:06:07.060 --> 01:06:09.620
- How much does he want?N- It makes no difference.


01:06:09.690 --> 01:06:13.150
- We've got to stop doing the trick.N- Stop the trick? Look at this.


01:06:13.230 --> 01:06:19.070
Last week they said you wereNthe premier stage performer in London.


01:06:19.140 --> 01:06:22.500
Not magician, mind you.NPerformer of any kind.


01:06:22.570 --> 01:06:25.800
- What's your point?N- My point is, you've climbed too high


01:06:25.880 --> 01:06:28.310
to get away withNprofessional embarrassment.


01:06:28.380 --> 01:06:31.750
We don't do any tricks we can't control.


01:06:33.920 --> 01:06:37.220
Just pay him for now. We keepNdoing the trick until Borden opens,


01:06:37.290 --> 01:06:39.260
and then we'll phase it out.


01:06:40.160 --> 01:06:41.650
All right.


01:06:44.430 --> 01:06:46.550
Cutter was always surprised


01:06:46.630 --> 01:06:48.530
how fast Root turned bad.


01:06:48.600 --> 01:06:53.160
To what do I owe the pleasureNof this rather welcome pint of ale?


01:06:53.240 --> 01:06:56.360
- You're the Great Danton, aren't you?N- Sh, sh, sh, sh, sh.


01:06:56.440 --> 01:07:00.100
Of course I am, but don't advertise it,Nbecause I'll be mobbed with fans.


01:07:00.180 --> 01:07:02.610
We paid him enoughNto keep him in beers.


01:07:02.680 --> 01:07:04.770
You wouldn't expect himNto rock the boat.


01:07:04.850 --> 01:07:07.440
Many of you may beNfamiliar with this technique,


01:07:07.520 --> 01:07:11.010
but for those of youNwho aren't, do not be alarmed.


01:07:11.090 --> 01:07:14.250
What you're about to seeNis considered safe.


01:07:14.320 --> 01:07:17.950
- And who are you?N- I am a humble admirer


01:07:18.030 --> 01:07:20.620
and a fellow practitioner.


01:07:20.700 --> 01:07:23.060
Mmm. Very good.


01:07:32.440 --> 01:07:35.280
- Another one?N- Oh, if you insist.


01:07:35.350 --> 01:07:38.080
- Another.N- I'm not performing tonight.


01:07:38.150 --> 01:07:40.170
I'm only doing one show,Nbut to be frank,


01:07:40.250 --> 01:07:42.580
my people pretty muchNrun things these days.


01:07:42.650 --> 01:07:43.850
Get up there.


01:07:45.220 --> 01:07:46.280
Get up!


01:07:46.360 --> 01:07:49.120
Your illusion, The Transported Man,


01:07:49.190 --> 01:07:51.790
I'm not claiming to know your methods,


01:07:51.860 --> 01:07:56.060
but I had a similar trick in my act,


01:07:56.130 --> 01:07:58.970
and, uh...I used a double.


01:07:59.040 --> 01:08:04.230
- Mm, I see, very good.N- Well, it was, and then it went bad.


01:08:04.310 --> 01:08:07.710
What I didn't count on was thatNwhen I incorporated this bloke


01:08:07.780 --> 01:08:09.870
into my act,


01:08:09.950 --> 01:08:11.940
he had complete power over me.


01:08:13.080 --> 01:08:14.710
Complete power, you say?


01:08:30.700 --> 01:08:32.130
Ohh!


01:08:32.200 --> 01:08:37.470
Be very careful givingNsomeone that power over you.


01:08:37.540 --> 01:08:41.870
Huh. Thank you. Um...


01:08:41.950 --> 01:08:44.810
Yes, thank you for the warning.


01:08:44.880 --> 01:08:47.580
Hmm. Cheers.


01:08:49.020 --> 01:08:51.150
I cannot claimNthis next feat as illusion.


01:08:51.220 --> 01:08:54.590
What you're about to seeNis considered safe.


01:08:58.900 --> 01:09:00.590
Ahh!


01:09:32.830 --> 01:09:37.790
Oh! The Great Danton.


01:09:44.010 --> 01:09:45.870
I apologize.


01:09:45.940 --> 01:09:49.710
There simply is too much magic...


01:09:49.780 --> 01:09:52.540
...for my stage at The Pantages


01:09:52.620 --> 01:09:54.780
across the street.


01:09:58.820 --> 01:10:01.760
Pardon my intrusion.


01:10:03.830 --> 01:10:08.230
And go easy on the poor chap.NHe does try so very hard.


01:10:11.100 --> 01:10:13.540
I don't know how Borden found him.


01:10:13.600 --> 01:10:15.500
Kept him under wraps. I was careful.


01:10:15.570 --> 01:10:17.230
Yeah, well, he did.


01:10:18.410 --> 01:10:20.400
Do you think it was her?


01:10:26.650 --> 01:10:29.620
You weren't expecting me?


01:10:29.690 --> 01:10:32.420
I expected you sooner.NYour message said afternoon.


01:10:32.490 --> 01:10:34.750
It takes a bit for meNto get around these days.


01:10:34.820 --> 01:10:38.890
He's taken everything from me.NMy wife, my career,


01:10:38.960 --> 01:10:40.830
- now you.N- You sent me.


01:10:40.900 --> 01:10:43.960
I sent you to steal his secret,Nnot to improve his act.


01:10:44.030 --> 01:10:45.590
- It's my job.N- Or fall in love!


01:10:45.670 --> 01:10:48.430
- I did everything you asked!N- Yes? Yes?


01:10:48.510 --> 01:10:50.100
- How does he do it?N- Cutter was right, a double.


01:10:51.070 --> 01:10:53.300
-'Course he said that.N- He didn't say it.


01:10:53.380 --> 01:10:56.810
I've seen things, makeup, glasses, wigs.NWe don't use for the show.


01:10:56.880 --> 01:10:59.610
- I've seen it hidden backstage.N- Misdirection.


01:10:59.680 --> 01:11:02.380
He leaves them lyingNaround to make you think that.


01:11:02.450 --> 01:11:04.320
He doesn't know when I'm looking.


01:11:04.390 --> 01:11:07.620
All the time, Olivia! That's who he is!


01:11:07.690 --> 01:11:08.950
That's what it takes!


01:11:09.030 --> 01:11:11.460
He lives his act, don't you see?


01:11:13.500 --> 01:11:16.860
Just because you're sleepingNwith him doesn't mean he trusts you.


01:11:16.930 --> 01:11:19.330
You think you can seeNeverything, don't you?


01:11:19.400 --> 01:11:22.240
The Great Danton is a blind fool.


01:11:22.310 --> 01:11:23.700
His notebook.


01:11:25.070 --> 01:11:27.340
You stole it?


01:11:27.410 --> 01:11:29.210
I borrowed it for tonight.


01:11:29.280 --> 01:11:31.470
I thought you could translateNsome of it...


01:11:31.550 --> 01:11:35.610
I can't. No one can. It's a cipher.


01:11:35.690 --> 01:11:39.120
Even with the keyword,Nit will take months to decode.


01:11:39.190 --> 01:11:42.090
- And without the keyword?N- Perhaps never.


01:11:42.160 --> 01:11:43.790
- We'll see.N- We will not see.


01:11:43.860 --> 01:11:46.800
If I don't get that back byNtomorrow he'll know I took it.


01:11:46.860 --> 01:11:49.160
- Leave him.N- I can't. He knows where I live.


01:11:50.500 --> 01:11:55.300
This is his diary, Olivia. All of hisNsecrets are right here in my hands.


01:11:55.970 --> 01:11:57.560
It won't bring your wife back.


01:11:57.640 --> 01:12:00.340
I don't care about my wife.NI care about his secret.


01:12:13.590 --> 01:12:16.320
Look, I'll, um...


01:12:16.390 --> 01:12:18.720
I'll go to his workshopNand stage a break-in.


01:12:18.800 --> 01:12:21.990
- He'll know you took it.N- Yes, me. Not you.


01:12:23.100 --> 01:12:25.090
Understand?


01:12:33.540 --> 01:12:34.530
Robert.


01:12:36.950 --> 01:12:39.740
I have fallen in love with him.


01:12:40.650 --> 01:12:43.120
Then I know how hardNthis has been for you.


01:12:51.660 --> 01:12:53.150
Notebook?


01:12:55.800 --> 01:12:57.790
Then he's just getting started.


01:13:27.030 --> 01:13:28.500
Professor!


01:13:28.560 --> 01:13:30.050
Good evening.


01:13:34.940 --> 01:13:36.560
I'm walking tonight.


01:13:36.640 --> 01:13:39.200
Let him come. I don't care.


01:13:39.280 --> 01:13:41.970
Professor! Professor!


01:15:04.360 --> 01:15:05.790
Ahh!


01:15:05.860 --> 01:15:08.420
- You all right?N- I'm alive.


01:15:08.500 --> 01:15:10.590
Saves me cutting you an air hole.


01:15:24.680 --> 01:15:27.240
- I'm impressed.N- Why is that?


01:15:27.320 --> 01:15:30.290
You're finally getting your hands dirty.


01:15:30.350 --> 01:15:33.250
It's what a good trick costs, Angier.


01:15:33.320 --> 01:15:36.120
Risk, sacrifice.


01:15:36.190 --> 01:15:38.680
The sacrifice, I'm afraid,Nis all gonna be yours,


01:15:38.760 --> 01:15:40.390
unless you give me what I want.


01:15:41.760 --> 01:15:43.890
- Which is?N- Your secret.


01:15:43.970 --> 01:15:45.370
My secret?


01:15:45.440 --> 01:15:48.560
Your method for The Transported Man.


01:15:48.640 --> 01:15:51.470
Fallon wouldn't tell me.NHe doesn't talk at all.


01:15:51.540 --> 01:15:55.030
- You have my notebook.N- Useless without the keyword.


01:15:56.510 --> 01:16:00.070
Write down your method,NMr. Borden, describe it in full.


01:16:13.200 --> 01:16:15.560
I want the whole method,Nnot the keyword.


01:16:15.630 --> 01:16:18.030
I don't know if your secret'sNin your notebook.


01:16:18.100 --> 01:16:20.570
The keyword is the method.


01:16:24.570 --> 01:16:25.870
Where's my ingénieur?


01:16:33.020 --> 01:16:35.640
- Alive?N- How fast can you dig?


01:16:38.120 --> 01:16:41.150
Fallon, you hear me? Fallon!


01:16:42.460 --> 01:16:45.120
- How's the arm?N- Still attached.


01:16:46.560 --> 01:16:48.120
Did you find your answer?


01:16:48.200 --> 01:16:51.960
Our answer, Cutter. I haven'tNlooked yet. I wanted you to share this.


01:16:52.030 --> 01:16:54.470
I already know how he does it, Robert.


01:16:54.540 --> 01:16:57.630
Same way he always has,Nthe same way as we do.


01:16:57.710 --> 01:17:00.180
It's just that you want something more.


01:17:00.240 --> 01:17:03.010
Well, let's find out then, shall we?


01:17:07.320 --> 01:17:08.750
What does it mean?


01:17:16.590 --> 01:17:19.060
It means, Cutter, we haveNa journey ahead of us.


01:17:19.130 --> 01:17:21.100
- To America.N- Robert?


01:17:22.060 --> 01:17:25.030
Listen to me.


01:17:25.100 --> 01:17:28.560
Obsession is a young man's game.


01:17:28.640 --> 01:17:30.160
Come on.


01:17:30.240 --> 01:17:32.710
I can't follow you any further in it.


01:17:33.780 --> 01:17:35.710
I can't, I'm sorry.


01:17:39.820 --> 01:17:41.510
Then the rest is up to me.


01:17:43.590 --> 01:17:45.110
I'm sorry.


01:17:50.430 --> 01:17:54.020
Good evening. Hello, darling.


01:17:54.100 --> 01:17:55.590
Champagne, your finest.


01:17:55.670 --> 01:17:58.360
I didn't know we were goingNto be joined for dinner.


01:17:58.430 --> 01:18:00.730
Absolutely, we are celebrating.


01:18:00.800 --> 01:18:02.500
Miss Wenscombe, Mr. Fallon.


01:18:03.510 --> 01:18:06.370
- What are we celebrating?N- We've hit upon a new trick.


01:18:06.440 --> 01:18:08.500
- Haven't we?N- What trick, Freddie?


01:18:08.580 --> 01:18:10.600
Yes, Freddie, what trick?


01:18:10.680 --> 01:18:15.080
I am going to buryNmyself alive every night,


01:18:15.150 --> 01:18:19.020
and then someone will come alongNand dig me up. Wonderful.


01:18:19.090 --> 01:18:22.180
- I think he's had quite enough...N- No, pour the champagne.


01:18:22.260 --> 01:18:25.960
Pour the... Sarah, don't talk to meNlike that. I'm not a bloody child.


01:18:26.030 --> 01:18:29.230
- Perhaps it would be better...N- Mr. Fallon, escort her home.


01:18:29.300 --> 01:18:32.130
- My husband's being a bore.N- Oh, please.


01:18:32.200 --> 01:18:36.000
- I see no reason you should suffer.N- Don't ruin this evening.


01:18:38.410 --> 01:18:41.310
Good night, Mrs. Borden.NGood night, Freddie.


01:18:45.750 --> 01:18:48.050
- Freddie?N- That's my name.


01:18:48.120 --> 01:18:51.480
- Not at home.N- I'm not always at home, am I?


01:18:53.290 --> 01:18:55.950
Couldn't you have at leastNtaken off the beard?


01:18:56.030 --> 01:19:00.190
Sarah, I just came fromNthe bloody theater just now.


01:19:00.260 --> 01:19:03.320
All right? I'm out in public.NEverybody else loves it.


01:19:03.400 --> 01:19:05.330
Why are you being like this?


01:19:05.400 --> 01:19:08.300
I had a terrible ordeal today.


01:19:08.370 --> 01:19:12.140
I thought thatNsomething very precious...


01:19:13.310 --> 01:19:15.240
...had been lost to me.


01:19:15.310 --> 01:19:18.440
So I just wantedNto celebrate just a little.


01:19:18.510 --> 01:19:21.970
All right, what? What did you lose?


01:19:27.120 --> 01:19:28.680
I see, more secrets.


01:19:29.630 --> 01:19:32.790
Sarah, secrets are my life.


01:19:34.730 --> 01:19:37.100
- Our life.N- No, Alfred, stop, this isn't you.


01:19:38.070 --> 01:19:40.540
Stop performing.


01:20:04.690 --> 01:20:07.190
I thought I had the place to myself.


01:20:07.260 --> 01:20:10.560
Unexpected guests, not very polite.


01:20:10.630 --> 01:20:12.460
A lot of questions.


01:20:12.540 --> 01:20:15.330
At first, I thought theyNworked for the government.


01:20:15.400 --> 01:20:19.070
- No?N- Worse, they work for Thomas Edison.


01:20:21.040 --> 01:20:23.530
Today, a mostNcurious development.


01:20:23.610 --> 01:20:26.670
His assistant came to usNwith a proposition.


01:20:28.320 --> 01:20:31.720
Obviously, Angier has sent herNand told her to admit as much.


01:20:31.790 --> 01:20:34.590
Does he enjoy takingNhis bows under the stage?


01:20:34.660 --> 01:20:38.420
He sent me here to steal your secrets,Nbut I've come to offer you his.


01:20:38.490 --> 01:20:41.460
This is the truth...


01:20:41.530 --> 01:20:42.520
...is it?


01:20:50.570 --> 01:20:54.030
No, that's what he toldNme to tell you. The truth...


01:20:54.110 --> 01:20:57.940
...is that I loved him and I stood byNhim and he sent me to you,


01:20:58.010 --> 01:21:01.540
like he would send a stagehandNto pick up his shirts.


01:21:01.620 --> 01:21:04.420
I hate him for that.


01:21:04.490 --> 01:21:07.720
I could spot Angier's methodsNfrom the back of the theater.


01:21:09.430 --> 01:21:11.690
So, what could youNpossibly have to offer me?


01:21:11.760 --> 01:21:13.390
You may know his tricks,


01:21:13.460 --> 01:21:16.520
but you can't understand whyNno one sees yours are better.


01:21:16.600 --> 01:21:19.160
You hide this.NI had to look very closely


01:21:19.240 --> 01:21:21.570
to spot itNduring The Transported Man,


01:21:21.640 --> 01:21:24.470
but this makes you unique.


01:21:24.540 --> 01:21:26.570
It shows you aren't using a double.


01:21:26.640 --> 01:21:29.130
You mustn't hide it.NYou must display it proudly.


01:21:29.210 --> 01:21:33.980
I'm sure it takes great skillNto perform illusions with one good hand.


01:21:34.050 --> 01:21:35.810
Yeah, it does.


01:21:37.590 --> 01:21:40.750
So let people know.


01:21:40.820 --> 01:21:44.320
You can be so much more thanNhe is and I can show you how.


01:21:46.030 --> 01:21:48.620
I thinkNshe's telling the truth.


01:21:48.700 --> 01:21:50.820
I think we cannot trust her.


01:21:54.370 --> 01:21:56.840
But I love her. I need her.


01:21:58.040 --> 01:22:01.370
To open myself to such a relationship,


01:22:01.440 --> 01:22:05.280
to the dangers of such an affair,


01:22:05.350 --> 01:22:10.150
I need assurances of fidelity, of love.


01:22:11.190 --> 01:22:12.780
But how to be sure?


01:22:14.990 --> 01:22:19.320
I know a way. It's the onlyNway to know her mind.


01:22:19.400 --> 01:22:21.230
How could he send you away?


01:22:23.100 --> 01:22:26.190
She must help meNrid ourselves of Angier.


01:22:32.810 --> 01:22:35.800
Today, my mistressNproves her truthfulness.


01:22:35.880 --> 01:22:37.610
Not to me, you understand.


01:22:37.680 --> 01:22:40.310
I've beenNconvinced since she led me to Root.


01:22:40.380 --> 01:22:43.910
Today, Olivia proves her love for me


01:22:43.990 --> 01:22:46.450
to you, Angier.


01:22:46.520 --> 01:22:50.930
Yes, Angier, she gave youNthis notebook at my request.


01:22:50.990 --> 01:22:54.430
And yes, "Tesla" is merelyNthe key to my dairy,


01:22:54.500 --> 01:22:57.290
not to my trick.NYou really think I'd part


01:22:57.370 --> 01:23:00.490
with my secret so easily after so much?


01:23:00.570 --> 01:23:02.230
Goodbye, Angier.


01:23:02.300 --> 01:23:04.670
May you find solaceNfor your forward ambition


01:23:04.740 --> 01:23:06.540
back in your American home.


01:23:16.050 --> 01:23:17.680
Tesla!


01:23:19.620 --> 01:23:22.020
Tesla! Alley!


01:23:23.230 --> 01:23:24.210
Alley!


01:23:24.290 --> 01:23:26.890
Tesla never made a machineNlike the one I asked for.


01:23:26.960 --> 01:23:29.760
- I never said he had.N- You let me believe that he had.


01:23:29.830 --> 01:23:32.530
You stole my money becauseNyour funding was cut off.


01:23:32.600 --> 01:23:35.500
You've been shootingNsparks in my top hat,


01:23:35.570 --> 01:23:39.060
Iaughing at me all along,Nwhile using my money to stave off ruin.


01:23:39.910 --> 01:23:42.040
- I have seen Edison's men.N- Where?


01:23:42.110 --> 01:23:44.600
In the hotel, I have a mindNto bring them up here.


01:23:44.680 --> 01:23:47.380
That would be unwise, Mr. Angier.


01:23:47.450 --> 01:23:50.580
It is true that you areNour last remaining financier,


01:23:50.650 --> 01:23:52.520
but we have not stolen your money.


01:23:52.590 --> 01:23:54.060
This is my cat.


01:23:54.120 --> 01:23:57.180
When I told you I could make youNa machine, I spoke a truth.


01:23:57.260 --> 01:23:58.350
Why isn't it working?


01:23:58.430 --> 01:24:00.760
Because exact science, Mr. Angier,


01:24:00.830 --> 01:24:02.230
is not an exact science.


01:24:02.300 --> 01:24:05.460
The machine simplyNdoes not operate as expected.


01:24:05.530 --> 01:24:09.560
- It requires further examination.N- So where did my top hat go?


01:24:09.640 --> 01:24:10.700
Nowhere.


01:24:10.770 --> 01:24:13.570
We tried the damn thing a dozen times.


01:24:13.640 --> 01:24:15.270
The hat went nowhere.


01:24:15.340 --> 01:24:17.240
We need to try different material.


01:24:17.310 --> 01:24:19.470
It may provoke a different result.


01:24:22.120 --> 01:24:23.680
Great.


01:24:30.830 --> 01:24:34.790
You are responsible for whateverNhappens to this animal, doctor.


01:24:56.320 --> 01:24:58.950
I hope whatever you wereNreally doing with my money


01:24:59.020 --> 01:25:01.460
was more worthwhile, Mr. Tesla.


01:25:57.380 --> 01:25:58.370
Alley!


01:26:01.450 --> 01:26:03.180
So the machine was working?


01:26:03.250 --> 01:26:06.880
I never checked the calibration,N'cause the hat never moved.


01:26:06.960 --> 01:26:09.820
These things never quiteNwork as you expect them to.


01:26:09.890 --> 01:26:12.380
That's one of the principalNbeauties of science.


01:26:12.460 --> 01:26:15.920
I'll need a couple of weeks to iron outNthe problems with the machine.


01:26:15.100 --> 01:26:18.060
We'll send word when it's ready.


01:26:20.270 --> 01:26:23.240
Don't forget your hat.


01:26:23.310 --> 01:26:27.040
- Well, which one is mine?N- They are all your hats.


01:26:32.980 --> 01:26:35.970
You look so prettyNin this new dress of yours.


01:26:36.050 --> 01:26:39.890
- Are we going to the zoo?N- No, Daddy has some errands to run.


01:26:39.960 --> 01:26:42.190
- But you promised.N- I promised, did I?


01:26:42.260 --> 01:26:44.560
Then go to the zoo, we shall.


01:26:44.630 --> 01:26:48.080
Daddy will go run his errands,Nand I'll be back before you know it.


01:26:48.160 --> 01:26:51.890
So you go get ready. We'll goNsee those chimpanzees.


01:26:54.900 --> 01:26:58.300
Sarah... what are you doing?


01:27:01.980 --> 01:27:04.970
Each of us have our vices.


01:27:08.080 --> 01:27:10.550
Sarah, whatever you may think...


01:27:12.120 --> 01:27:15.750
...your only competitionNfor my affections is our little girl.


01:27:15.820 --> 01:27:18.790
I love you. I will always love you


01:27:18.860 --> 01:27:20.290
and you alone.


01:27:22.160 --> 01:27:25.960
- You mean it today.N- Absolutely.


01:27:26.030 --> 01:27:29.870
Which makes it so muchNharder when you don't.


01:27:39.210 --> 01:27:42.010
More shopping. She doesNlove the smell of money.


01:27:42.080 --> 01:27:46.380
The little lady wants to go to the zoo,Nso I thought you could take her, yeah?


01:27:46.460 --> 01:27:48.820
I mean, I can do it tomorrow, if not.


01:27:48.890 --> 01:27:52.190
And, uh... Sarah,


01:27:52.260 --> 01:27:54.390
she knows.


01:27:54.460 --> 01:27:58.630
Uh, at least she knowsNthat something is not right,


01:27:58.700 --> 01:28:01.600
so if you can just doNwhatever you can to help me.


01:28:01.670 --> 01:28:06.230
Talk to her, justNconvince her that I do love her.


01:28:16.890 --> 01:28:18.850
What is it, Freddie?


01:28:18.920 --> 01:28:21.220
Listen, don't call me that, please.


01:28:21.290 --> 01:28:25.160
It's nothing. It's just thatNsometimes it seems wrong.


01:28:25.230 --> 01:28:27.720
I told you, when you'reNwith me, you're with me.


01:28:27.800 --> 01:28:30.820
Leave your family at homeNwhere they belong.


01:28:30.900 --> 01:28:34.160
I'm trying. I'm trying, Olivia.


01:28:34.240 --> 01:28:36.600
- I'll get dressed.N- Yeah.


01:28:38.110 --> 01:28:41.130
I saw Fallon hanging around again.


01:28:41.210 --> 01:28:43.680
There's something aboutNthat man I don't trust.


01:28:43.750 --> 01:28:46.810
You trust me? Then trust Fallon.


01:28:46.880 --> 01:28:49.540
He protects the thingsNthat I care about.


01:29:27.790 --> 01:29:30.280
We're sorry to see you go, Mr. Angier.


01:29:30.360 --> 01:29:32.920
We were sorry to seeNMr. Tesla leave, as well.


01:29:32.100 --> 01:29:35.090
He's very good to Colorado Springs.


01:29:35.160 --> 01:29:37.830
Mr. Angier,


01:29:37.900 --> 01:29:41.530
I didn't think it was necessaryNto tell Edison's men about the box.


01:29:41.600 --> 01:29:43.260
What box?


01:30:08.600 --> 01:30:11.100
I apologize for leavingNwithout saying goodbye.


01:30:12.070 --> 01:30:17.300
But I seem to have outstayedNmy welcome in Colorado.


01:30:17.370 --> 01:30:21.870
The truly extraordinary is notNpermitted in science and industry.


01:30:21.940 --> 01:30:24.740
Perhaps you'll findNmore luck in your field,


01:30:24.810 --> 01:30:27.480
where people are happy to be mystified.


01:30:27.550 --> 01:30:31.510
You will find what youNare looking for in this box.


01:30:31.590 --> 01:30:36.020
Alley has written youNa thorough set of instructions.


01:30:36.090 --> 01:30:40.820
I add only one suggestionNon using the machine.


01:30:40.900 --> 01:30:42.860
Destroy it.


01:30:42.930 --> 01:30:46.230
Drop it to the bottomNof the deepest ocean.


01:30:46.300 --> 01:30:49.700
Such a thing will bring you only misery.


01:30:53.580 --> 01:30:57.200
Tesla's warning isNas unheeded as he knew it would be.


01:30:57.280 --> 01:31:00.840
Today I tested the machine.NTaking precautions in case


01:31:00.920 --> 01:31:03.890
Tesla hadn't ironed outNthe kinks in its operation.


01:31:03.950 --> 01:31:05.750
But if it went wrong,


01:31:05.820 --> 01:31:07.980
I would not want to liveNlike that for long.


01:31:27.440 --> 01:31:31.570
But here at the turn,NI must leave you, Borden.


01:31:31.650 --> 01:31:33.880
Yes, you, Borden,


01:31:33.950 --> 01:31:36.320
sitting there in your cell,


01:31:36.390 --> 01:31:40.410
reading my diary, awaiting your death,


01:31:40.490 --> 01:31:42.480
for my murder.


01:31:47.830 --> 01:31:51.130
Angier's journal, that gestureNof good faith, that's a fake.


01:31:51.200 --> 01:31:52.500
I assure you, it's not.


01:31:52.570 --> 01:31:55.500
The provenance of the journalNis clear and under no doubt.


01:31:55.570 --> 01:32:00.060
And it's written in Angier's own hand,Nfor which we have numerous examples.


01:32:01.940 --> 01:32:03.840
It don't matter.


01:32:05.780 --> 01:32:07.810
So my tricks.


01:32:11.050 --> 01:32:14.510
- All of them.N- Including The Transported Man?


01:32:15.960 --> 01:32:19.150
- Lord Caldlow will be very pleased.N- No, he won't.


01:32:19.230 --> 01:32:21.590
They're not complete.


01:32:21.660 --> 01:32:24.390
It's just the pledgeNand the turn for each.


01:32:24.470 --> 01:32:28.530
Without the prestige for theseNtricks, these are worthless.


01:32:28.600 --> 01:32:30.630
Yeah.


01:32:30.710 --> 01:32:34.230
You get the rest of it...Nwhen you bring my daughter here.


01:32:36.980 --> 01:32:39.210
I want to say goodbye.


01:32:40.950 --> 01:32:44.110
We have to go through it now.NWe have to go through it now.


01:32:44.190 --> 01:32:46.550
Now, listen to me, deny it all you want.


01:32:46.620 --> 01:32:48.990
Olivia means nothing.


01:32:49.060 --> 01:32:50.850
- Olivia?N- I need an assistant.


01:32:50.930 --> 01:32:53.760
- I'll go to her, I'll tell her.N- You'll tell her what?


01:32:53.830 --> 01:32:55.890
I know what you really are, Alfred.


01:32:57.100 --> 01:32:59.760
- I know.N- Sarah, Sarah, Sarah.


01:32:59.840 --> 01:33:02.460
- I can't keep it in.N- You can't talk like this.


01:33:02.540 --> 01:33:05.060
- No. No.N- Sarah, shut up! Sarah, shut up!


01:33:05.140 --> 01:33:09.270
I don't want to hear it anymore.NYou can't talk like this.


01:33:11.880 --> 01:33:15.280
You can't hide it anymore,Nbecause I know, Alfred, I know.


01:33:15.350 --> 01:33:18.790
I know what you really are, Alfred.


01:33:18.850 --> 01:33:21.650
I can't live like this.


01:33:21.720 --> 01:33:23.850
Oh, well, you thinkNI can live like this?


01:33:23.930 --> 01:33:27.090
You think I bloody enjoyNliving like this?


01:33:27.160 --> 01:33:31.570
We have this beautiful house,Nlovely little girl, we're married.


01:33:31.630 --> 01:33:33.290
What is so wrong with your life?


01:33:33.370 --> 01:33:35.960
Alfred, I can't live like this!


01:33:36.040 --> 01:33:38.400
Well, what do you want from me?


01:33:41.740 --> 01:33:45.440
I... I want...


01:33:45.510 --> 01:33:48.570
I want you to be... honest with me.


01:33:51.320 --> 01:33:53.790
No tricks.


01:33:53.860 --> 01:33:55.950
No lies.


01:33:56.020 --> 01:33:59.820
And no secrets.


01:34:06.100 --> 01:34:09.430
Do you... do you love me?


01:34:12.510 --> 01:34:14.130
Not today.


01:34:16.280 --> 01:34:17.340
No.


01:35:55.010 --> 01:35:56.030
Who's there?


01:35:59.180 --> 01:36:01.270
I'm looking for an old friend.


01:36:01.350 --> 01:36:04.280
I heard about a booking,Nnice little theater,


01:36:04.350 --> 01:36:06.790
- good up-and-coming magician.N- You're back.


01:36:06.860 --> 01:36:08.450
It's good to see you, John.


01:36:09.220 --> 01:36:11.950
Good rehearsal space.


01:36:12.030 --> 01:36:14.790
Blind stagehands, I like it.


01:36:14.860 --> 01:36:17.530
You always had a good eye for publicity.


01:36:17.600 --> 01:36:18.930
I need your help, John.


01:36:19.000 --> 01:36:21.800
It's my last show. A limited engagement.


01:36:21.870 --> 01:36:23.500
Your last show?


01:36:23.570 --> 01:36:27.700
A wise man once told me obsessionNwas a young man's game.


01:36:27.780 --> 01:36:31.340
I'm almost done. There's one thing left.


01:36:32.350 --> 01:36:34.870
The Real Transported Man.


01:36:36.690 --> 01:36:38.680
You want to design a show around it?


01:36:38.750 --> 01:36:41.620
I don't want you backstageNI need you in front managing.


01:36:41.690 --> 01:36:44.350
Call in any favorsNor connections you have left


01:36:44.430 --> 01:36:45.890
to get us the right booking.


01:36:45.960 --> 01:36:48.050
What sort of booking you after?


01:36:48.130 --> 01:36:50.530
The sort that Borden can't ignore.


01:36:56.910 --> 01:37:00.140
Oh, what an honor it isNto see you again, sir.


01:37:00.210 --> 01:37:04.170
You told me you only wanted to show meNone trick that'd pique my interest.


01:37:04.250 --> 01:37:07.410
- It's a very clever trick.N- Pleased to meet you, Mr. Ackerman.


01:37:07.480 --> 01:37:10.350
Likewise, I'm sure.NLet's get on, shall we?


01:37:13.990 --> 01:37:15.750
Turn it on, gentlemen.


01:37:20.100 --> 01:37:22.120
Very pretty.


01:37:33.170 --> 01:37:36.840
That's it, Cutter? He simply disappears?


01:37:36.910 --> 01:37:39.280
That's not a trick. He has to come back.


01:37:39.350 --> 01:37:41.510
- There has to be a...N- A prestige?


01:37:41.580 --> 01:37:42.570
Exactly.


01:37:45.590 --> 01:37:48.250
Pardon me.


01:37:48.320 --> 01:37:51.590
It's very rare to see...


01:37:51.660 --> 01:37:53.130
...real magic.


01:37:54.630 --> 01:37:56.320
It's been many years since...


01:37:56.400 --> 01:37:58.130
Are you interested in helping us?


01:38:00.200 --> 01:38:03.930
Yes... but you'll haveNto dress it up a little.


01:38:06.210 --> 01:38:07.870
Disguise it.


01:38:09.540 --> 01:38:12.040
Give them enough reason to doubt it.


01:38:12.850 --> 01:38:16.080
You haven't spokenNabout her, Freddie, not once.


01:38:16.150 --> 01:38:19.850
Why would I talk about her to you, hm?


01:38:19.920 --> 01:38:23.790
Because she was a part ofNyour life and now she's gone.


01:38:26.760 --> 01:38:31.260
You know, the day before she killedNherself she said she wanted to meet me.


01:38:31.330 --> 01:38:34.270
That she had somethingNto tell me about you.


01:38:34.340 --> 01:38:37.930
I was such a coward,NI couldn't bring myself to face her.


01:38:38.010 --> 01:38:39.500
But...


01:38:40.710 --> 01:38:42.970
...what would she have said?


01:38:43.040 --> 01:38:46.140
You want to know the truth about me?


01:38:47.420 --> 01:38:49.910
The truth is that...


01:38:52.090 --> 01:38:54.080
...I never loved Sarah.


01:38:55.290 --> 01:38:56.780
I never loved her.


01:38:56.860 --> 01:38:59.090
You married her,Nyou had a child with her.


01:38:59.160 --> 01:39:02.250
Yes. Part of me. Part of me did, but...


01:39:02.330 --> 01:39:04.260
...the other part didn't.


01:39:04.330 --> 01:39:08.560
The part that found you,Nthe part that's sitting here right now.


01:39:08.640 --> 01:39:11.700
I love you. No, Olivia, I love you.


01:39:11.770 --> 01:39:13.740
That's the truth.


01:39:13.810 --> 01:39:16.210
That is the truth that matters.


01:39:16.280 --> 01:39:20.680
You could be in some other restaurantNwith some other woman right now,


01:39:20.750 --> 01:39:22.340
talking about me that way.


01:39:22.420 --> 01:39:24.540
- No.N- Yes.


01:39:27.990 --> 01:39:31.720
It's inhuman to be so cold.


01:39:37.400 --> 01:39:38.660
He's back.


01:39:39.570 --> 01:39:42.830
After two years, he's got a new trick.


01:39:42.900 --> 01:39:45.570
They're saying it'sNthe best London's ever seen.


01:39:47.780 --> 01:39:50.240
You should see the lookNon your face, Professor.


01:39:52.110 --> 01:39:54.050
You should go to him.


01:39:54.120 --> 01:39:56.640
You two deserve each other.


01:40:01.620 --> 01:40:05.560
But I'm afraid I'm booked. The MoscowNBallet plays through next year.


01:40:05.630 --> 01:40:10.190
Then get rid of them. There will beN100 performances, no more, no less.


01:40:10.270 --> 01:40:12.760
Five performances a week, no matinees.


01:40:14.570 --> 01:40:17.600
That's what you'llNcharge for each ticket. Good day.


01:40:40.330 --> 01:40:44.960
Ladies and gentlemen, my first trick ofNthe evening involves considerable risk.


01:40:46.200 --> 01:40:47.570
Anyone in the audience


01:40:47.640 --> 01:40:50.470
who would be irrevocablyNdamaged by seeing a man drown


01:40:50.540 --> 01:40:52.130
should leave now.


01:40:52.210 --> 01:40:55.000
When I tell you the ladyNwho taught me this illusion


01:40:55.080 --> 01:40:57.070
actually died performing it,


01:40:57.150 --> 01:41:00.440
you'll understand the seriousnessNof the dangers involved.


01:41:02.620 --> 01:41:05.020
Let's begin.


01:41:14.730 --> 01:41:17.360
In my travels, I have seen the future.


01:41:19.170 --> 01:41:22.760
And it is a strange future, indeed.


01:41:22.840 --> 01:41:24.100
The world, ladies and gentlemen,


01:41:25.070 --> 01:41:27.370
is on the brink of new


01:41:27.440 --> 01:41:29.170
and terrifying possibilities.


01:41:49.660 --> 01:41:53.120
What you're about to witnessNis not magic.


01:41:54.300 --> 01:41:55.700
It's purely science.


01:41:55.770 --> 01:41:58.200
I'd like to invite youNto come up on stage now


01:41:58.270 --> 01:42:01.260
so that you can examineNthe machine for yourselves.


01:42:56.560 --> 01:42:58.400
Man's reach


01:42:58.470 --> 01:43:01.590
exceeds his imagination.


01:43:12.880 --> 01:43:14.250
Bravo!


01:43:22.290 --> 01:43:25.020
One hundred performances. Why?


01:43:25.090 --> 01:43:26.650
Does his method dictate that?


01:43:26.730 --> 01:43:28.630
Is it a publicity move? What is it?


01:43:28.700 --> 01:43:31.060
He's a no-talent magician,Nand they call him


01:43:31.130 --> 01:43:33.530
the bloody best in England. Why?


01:43:33.600 --> 01:43:36.370
Fifty yards in a second! In a second!


01:43:36.440 --> 01:43:39.530
And all that we knowNis he uses a trap door.


01:43:39.610 --> 01:43:43.870
Brilliant! What is going onNunder that stage? Huh?!


01:43:43.950 --> 01:43:46.380
Why can't you out-think him?


01:44:01.500 --> 01:44:06.700
They do this every night,Nafter each performance. Yeah?


01:44:32.990 --> 01:44:34.330
Huh.


01:44:35.200 --> 01:44:38.170
We're done.


01:44:39.470 --> 01:44:41.030
All right?


01:44:42.340 --> 01:44:44.100
Let him have his trick.


01:44:44.170 --> 01:44:46.660
I don't need his secret.


01:44:46.740 --> 01:44:48.230
So...


01:44:49.740 --> 01:44:52.710
...don't go back there,Nyou leave him alone.


01:44:52.780 --> 01:44:56.050
Both of us... just leave him alone.


01:44:56.120 --> 01:44:57.740
We're done.


01:45:06.490 --> 01:45:08.550
I told you, John.


01:45:08.630 --> 01:45:10.720
I don't want you backstage on this one.


01:45:12.370 --> 01:45:14.770
I would like toNinvite you onstage now


01:45:14.840 --> 01:45:17.530
so that you can examineNthe machine for yourselves.


01:45:46.730 --> 01:45:50.470
- Hey, where do you think...?N- I'm part of the bloody act, you fool.


01:45:59.480 --> 01:46:00.470
Who was that?


01:46:57.040 --> 01:47:01.170
Hey! Where's the bloody key?!


01:47:01.240 --> 01:47:02.800
Where's the bloody key?!


01:47:05.250 --> 01:47:08.980
Where's the bloody key?!NHe's bloody drowning!


01:47:18.230 --> 01:47:19.210
Hold on!


01:47:24.530 --> 01:47:25.100
What have you done?


01:47:47.820 --> 01:47:53.260
Alfred Borden, you have been foundNguilty of the murder of Robert Angier.


01:47:53.330 --> 01:47:57.560
You will be hangedNby the neck until dead.


01:47:57.630 --> 01:48:00.600
May the Lord have mercy on your soul.


01:48:02.370 --> 01:48:04.530
Mr. Cutter?


01:48:04.610 --> 01:48:06.230
Owens.


01:48:06.310 --> 01:48:09.140
Oh, thank you for coming, Mr. Owens.


01:48:09.210 --> 01:48:13.580
It has fallen to me to disposeNof Mr. Angier's equipment.


01:48:13.650 --> 01:48:15.240
But I notice from this manifest


01:48:15.320 --> 01:48:19.010
that Lord Caldlow has purchasedNthe bulk of the items.


01:48:19.090 --> 01:48:22.390
Mr. Cutter, if you need to knowNwhere to deliver these items...


01:48:22.460 --> 01:48:26.050
No, it's just there isNone particular item,


01:48:26.990 --> 01:48:29.590
this item, in fact,


01:48:29.660 --> 01:48:31.930
- I would like to...N- You would like to...


01:48:31.100 --> 01:48:33.090
...buy.


01:48:33.170 --> 01:48:35.070
- Buy yourself?N- Yeah, I suppose so.


01:48:36.300 --> 01:48:38.240
- This is the machine?N- Yes.


01:48:38.310 --> 01:48:40.540
Well, I'm afraidNLord Caldlow was adamant


01:48:40.610 --> 01:48:42.840
about purchasing this particular item.


01:48:42.910 --> 01:48:46.000
Do you think I couldNtalk to Lord Caldlow in person?


01:48:46.080 --> 01:48:48.840
Out of the question, I'm afraid.


01:48:51.290 --> 01:48:53.190
Of course,


01:48:53.250 --> 01:48:56.490
I suppose if, in the courseNof your delivery arrangements,


01:48:56.560 --> 01:49:01.020
your paths were to cross,NI can't stop you speaking your mind.


01:49:01.100 --> 01:49:03.120
Thank you.


01:49:04.700 --> 01:49:06.860
- Still here, Borden?N- For now.


01:49:07.470 --> 01:49:10.440
You got a visitor. Lord Caldlow.


01:49:10.500 --> 01:49:12.600
With a little girl.


01:49:20.880 --> 01:49:22.780
Jess?


01:49:22.850 --> 01:49:24.480
Hello, my love.


01:49:24.550 --> 01:49:28.010
How are you? I've missed you so much.


01:49:28.090 --> 01:49:30.220
Fallon's missed you too. We both have.


01:49:30.290 --> 01:49:32.620
Daddy, can I come in there?


01:49:33.260 --> 01:49:35.890
Not right now. Not right now, darling.


01:49:35.960 --> 01:49:38.230
No, but everythingNis gonna be all right.


01:49:39.800 --> 01:49:41.530
You must be Lord Caldlow?


01:49:41.600 --> 01:49:45.330
Caldlow. Yes, I am. I always have been.


01:49:50.380 --> 01:49:52.570
They flatter you with all those chains.


01:49:52.650 --> 01:49:55.670
Don't they know you can't escapeNwithout your rubber ball?


01:49:55.750 --> 01:49:58.740
I pulled you out... out of that tank.


01:49:58.820 --> 01:50:02.650
All I wanted to do was proveNthat I was a better magician.


01:50:02.720 --> 01:50:04.620
But you couldn't leave me alone.


01:50:06.130 --> 01:50:08.220
I don't know what you've done.


01:50:10.130 --> 01:50:13.830
But you're not afraid to getNyour hands dirty anymore, are you?


01:50:13.900 --> 01:50:17.170
No, not anymore. And I win.


01:50:17.240 --> 01:50:20.570
No one cares about the manNin the box, the man who disappears.


01:50:20.640 --> 01:50:21.770
You win?


01:50:23.210 --> 01:50:27.870
This ain't a bloody competitionNanymore. This is my little girl's life.


01:50:27.950 --> 01:50:30.940
And don't you dareNput her in the middle of this.


01:50:31.020 --> 01:50:34.010
Oh, I know how hard it isNto have someone so special


01:50:34.090 --> 01:50:36.450
taken away from you, don't I, Borden?


01:50:37.460 --> 01:50:40.190
And you can't take itNwith you, now, can you?


01:50:40.260 --> 01:50:42.160
Oh, she'll be looked after.


01:50:42.230 --> 01:50:44.250
Goodbye, Professor. Come on, darling.


01:50:44.330 --> 01:50:46.090
No, no, no, no, stop, my darling.


01:50:46.170 --> 01:50:48.290
Look, here.


01:50:49.840 --> 01:50:53.100
That's what you're after.NThat's what this is about.


01:50:53.910 --> 01:50:55.270
Take it.


01:50:55.340 --> 01:50:57.040
- Your secret?N- Yeah.


01:51:00.250 --> 01:51:03.810
You always were the better magician.NWe both know that.


01:51:04.450 --> 01:51:07.050
Whatever your secret was,Nyou have to agree,


01:51:08.190 --> 01:51:09.520
mine is better.


01:51:11.230 --> 01:51:14.590
Don't do this. Don't do this,NAngier. Jess, Jess!


01:51:14.660 --> 01:51:18.190
Jess, I'm gonna take youNhome soon. I promise.


01:51:18.270 --> 01:51:20.830
- For God's sake.N- I promise. Look!


01:51:24.670 --> 01:51:28.270
I promise. I love you, Jess.


01:51:28.340 --> 01:51:30.000
I love you.


01:51:30.080 --> 01:51:31.700
- Come on.N- I love you.


01:51:31.780 --> 01:51:33.470
I love you, Jess.


01:51:33.550 --> 01:51:35.880
Angier! Angier!


01:51:35.950 --> 01:51:38.040
What, do you thinkNthis place can hold me?


01:51:38.120 --> 01:51:41.140
Angier! They're gonna bloody hang me!


01:51:41.220 --> 01:51:43.750
And you can put a stop to this now!


01:51:44.390 --> 01:51:46.590
Listen! Listen! That man...


01:51:46.660 --> 01:51:49.030
Listen, that man isNthe one I'm in for killing!


01:51:49.100 --> 01:51:53.430
Listen! If he's alive, I'm not guilty!


01:51:53.500 --> 01:51:55.760
- I'm not guilty!N- I don't care!


01:51:55.840 --> 01:51:57.930
- Get hold of him.N- Angier!


01:52:02.610 --> 01:52:05.170
Run along now.


01:52:05.250 --> 01:52:07.770
Sir, there's a gentleman waiting.


01:52:24.600 --> 01:52:27.330
- Dear God.N- Hello, Cutter.


01:52:28.300 --> 01:52:30.740
You're still alive.


01:52:30.800 --> 01:52:32.670
How is it you're still alive?


01:52:32.740 --> 01:52:35.140
I saw you on a slab, for God's sake.


01:52:38.150 --> 01:52:40.170
- Child.N- Good night, sir.


01:52:40.250 --> 01:52:42.220
Good night, Jess.


01:52:43.450 --> 01:52:45.110
I've seen her before.


01:52:45.190 --> 01:52:47.710
I saw her in court with...


01:52:48.660 --> 01:52:50.280
...Fallon.


01:52:52.390 --> 01:52:54.990
- What have you done?N- She needs looking after.


01:52:55.060 --> 01:52:57.550
She needs her father.


01:52:57.630 --> 01:53:00.600
You're letting him hang,Nand I helped you.


01:53:00.670 --> 01:53:05.610
I came here to beg Lord CaldlowNto let me destroy that machine.


01:53:07.070 --> 01:53:10.510
I am not going to beg you for anything.


01:53:10.580 --> 01:53:13.840
You don't have to. I'm gonnaNmake sure it is never used again.


01:53:14.980 --> 01:53:18.080
Then, Lord Caldlow...


01:53:20.620 --> 01:53:22.680
...where do you want me to deliver it?


01:53:22.760 --> 01:53:26.520
My theater. It belongsNwith the prestige materials.


01:53:26.990 --> 01:53:29.590
John, I tried not to involve you.


01:53:42.540 --> 01:53:44.810
So...


01:53:46.850 --> 01:53:49.440
We go alone now.


01:53:49.520 --> 01:53:51.950
Both of us.


01:53:54.760 --> 01:53:58.160
I mean, I don't haveNas far to go as you.


01:54:03.460 --> 01:54:04.800
No.


01:54:06.330 --> 01:54:09.390
You were right. I should haveNleft him to his damn trick.


01:54:11.170 --> 01:54:13.260
I'm sorry.


01:54:14.810 --> 01:54:17.140
I'm sorry for a lot of things.


01:54:18.280 --> 01:54:21.010
I'm sorry about Sarah.


01:54:22.120 --> 01:54:25.570
Didn't mean to hurt her, I didn't.


01:54:27.450 --> 01:54:31.790
You go live your life in full now,Nall right? You live for both of us.


01:54:40.630 --> 01:54:42.120
Goodbye.


01:55:27.920 --> 01:55:30.350
Are you watching closely?


01:56:01.720 --> 01:56:03.650
Put it down on the end.


01:56:37.050 --> 01:56:40.820
Take a minute to considerNyour achievement.


01:56:41.890 --> 01:56:44.690
I once told you about a sailor


01:56:44.760 --> 01:56:47.060
who described drowning to me.


01:56:47.130 --> 01:56:49.320
Yes, he said it was like going home.


01:56:50.430 --> 01:56:54.200
I was lying. He said it was agony.


01:57:33.940 --> 01:57:38.110
Alfred Borden, this day,Nin the name of the king


01:57:38.180 --> 01:57:40.170
and the High Court of England,


01:57:40.250 --> 01:57:42.080
you will meet your end.


01:57:44.180 --> 01:57:46.210
No one cares about the man in the box.


01:57:51.060 --> 01:57:52.790
Cutter?


01:57:57.460 --> 01:57:58.990
Cutter!


01:58:00.870 --> 01:58:03.130
Do you have anything to say?


01:58:07.870 --> 01:58:09.270
Abracadabra.


01:58:45.910 --> 01:58:48.640
A brother? A twin?


01:58:50.480 --> 01:58:52.850
You were Fallon.


01:58:54.350 --> 01:58:57.020
- The whole time?N- No.


01:58:58.060 --> 01:59:00.390
We were both Fallon.


01:59:00.460 --> 01:59:02.360
We were both Borden.


01:59:07.730 --> 01:59:10.700
Were you the one who went into the box?


01:59:10.770 --> 01:59:12.470
Or the one who came back out?


01:59:13.770 --> 01:59:16.070
We took turns.


01:59:20.880 --> 01:59:22.940
The trick is where we would swap.


01:59:29.160 --> 01:59:31.060
Cutter knew. Cutter knew.


01:59:31.120 --> 01:59:33.390
But I told him it wasNtoo simple, too easy.


01:59:34.590 --> 01:59:35.580
No.


01:59:37.130 --> 01:59:39.100
Simple, maybe, but not easy.


01:59:39.170 --> 01:59:42.930
There's nothing easyNabout two men sharing one life.


01:59:48.610 --> 01:59:51.810
I don't understand,Nhow it can be bleeding again?


01:59:55.280 --> 01:59:58.080
Wha... What about Olivia and your wife?


01:59:59.090 --> 02:00:00.990
We each loved one of them.


02:00:04.620 --> 02:00:07.350
I loved Sarah.


02:00:07.430 --> 02:00:09.950
He loved Olivia.


02:00:10.030 --> 02:00:12.460
We each had half of a full life,


02:00:12.530 --> 02:00:15.520
really, which was enough for us...


02:00:15.600 --> 02:00:16.590
...just.


02:00:19.240 --> 02:00:20.970
But not for them.


02:00:23.540 --> 02:00:25.770
See, sacrifice, Robert,


02:00:25.850 --> 02:00:28.580
that's the price of a good trick.


02:00:30.620 --> 02:00:33.180
You wouldn't knowNanything about that, would you?


02:00:36.460 --> 02:00:38.390
I've... I've made sacrifices.


02:00:38.460 --> 02:00:40.430
- No.N- Yes.


02:00:40.890 --> 02:00:43.990
It takes nothingNto steal another man's work.


02:00:44.060 --> 02:00:46.830
Yeah, it takes everything.


02:01:06.890 --> 02:01:09.010
No, no, wait, I'm not...


02:01:15.700 --> 02:01:18.320
It took courage.


02:01:20.330 --> 02:01:23.530
It took courage to climbNinto that machine every night,


02:01:24.340 --> 02:01:26.770
not knowing...


02:01:26.840 --> 02:01:28.970
...if I'd be the man in the box...


02:01:32.010 --> 02:01:33.270
...or in the prestige.


02:01:34.610 --> 02:01:37.640
Do you want to see...


02:01:37.720 --> 02:01:40.020
...what it cost me?


02:01:40.090 --> 02:01:42.850
You didn't see where you are, did you?


02:01:43.760 --> 02:01:46.160
Look. Look.


02:01:47.260 --> 02:01:48.750
I don't care.


02:01:53.470 --> 02:01:57.030
You went halfway around the world.


02:01:57.100 --> 02:01:59.870
You spent a fortune.


02:02:01.940 --> 02:02:04.470
You did terrible things.


02:02:05.480 --> 02:02:07.950
Really terrible things, Robert.


02:02:09.980 --> 02:02:11.470
And all for nothing.


02:02:12.450 --> 02:02:13.650
For nothing?


02:02:13.720 --> 02:02:15.050
Yeah.


02:02:18.730 --> 02:02:21.350
You never understood...


02:02:21.430 --> 02:02:23.420
...why we did this.


02:02:26.530 --> 02:02:29.090
The audience knows the truth.


02:02:30.240 --> 02:02:32.670
The world is simple.


02:02:32.740 --> 02:02:34.470
It's miserable.


02:02:34.540 --> 02:02:38.240
Solid... Solid all the way through.


02:02:40.580 --> 02:02:42.910
But if you could fool them,


02:02:42.980 --> 02:02:45.140
even for a second...


02:02:46.690 --> 02:02:49.090
...then you could make them wonder.


02:02:50.220 --> 02:02:52.420
And then you...


02:02:52.490 --> 02:02:54.720
Then you got to see something


02:02:54.790 --> 02:02:56.460
very special.


02:03:00.770 --> 02:03:03.290
You really don't know.


02:03:06.370 --> 02:03:08.030
It was...


02:03:09.110 --> 02:03:12.080
...it was the look on their faces.


02:03:27.260 --> 02:03:32.100
Every magic trickNconsists of three parts, or acts.


02:03:35.540 --> 02:03:38.990
The first part is called "the pledge".


02:03:39.070 --> 02:03:41.840
The magician shows youNsomething ordinary.


02:03:42.980 --> 02:03:45.910
The second act is called "the turn".


02:03:47.380 --> 02:03:50.250
The magician takesNthe ordinary something


02:03:50.320 --> 02:03:53.180
and makes it intoNsomething extraordinary.


02:03:54.520 --> 02:03:58.420
But you wouldn't clap yet,Nbecause making something disappear


02:03:58.490 --> 02:04:02.590
isn't enough. You have to bring it back.


02:04:37.030 --> 02:04:39.460
Now you're looking for the secret.


02:04:42.400 --> 02:04:46.130
But you won't find it, because,Nof course, you're not really looking.


02:04:49.240 --> 02:04:52.680
You don't really want to work it out.


02:04:55.480 --> 02:04:57.780
You want to be fooled.

